Ãª£⁄<ﬂ˜s<‘çXº~4Ω~f4ª␀πºÙ3 ∫∂-íªæ˛Gº‘“˛ª|X =Ã˙>ºˆ„;∆˘Äª∑æË;≤À>ΩíîºàÑüª@¨¨<ﬁÈ_;Njº8 º≥î¨ºvúàªl√√<r:5<yø:º ∫ä<—j¶<ûù¸ºIãˆ∫#k<ﬁƒ<_¡;¥]ª©}K<ÏÂ÷;◊⁄ΩIº=óIÑºùú<8ì<à…Eºî¸Nª»<ºll;µd$ºSÁ˝ºÌiªX∑:=«<±ƒ¥ª#‰∆ªAnêºäTó=ØÌ≤;|X =Ú"ΩOΩA<7	Ω—j¶<‚ˇºP|<W´<ëŸúºå+ô<UyŸ<ﬂ≤M<9∏}º≈»sº¨—
Ωg◊#ºIãv<Oqë:.N‚<wË∏∫!œ®<1‡Ω:;˛(<?/Ôªs£;…hcº/¢º6,Ω~mæ∫ÖÎ9Ωø\=må±º‡/<√ÒÒ∫ló∫ÎTÄ∫ø{ÖºDòÃ9Óºÿ;q,!<@gÜ<ﬁùØº˙Ô·ºB¡J<(◊ºäÂÌºOËºÖ7jΩ~≤d<4Ä-ºéÖ]<XP€ºùJBªƒ)	ºøQºçw…º}§–<•›€ºi1Ë;_’‡<ˇQµªØ®<Ô Ï;{"title": "VITAMINA B2:Vitamin B2, also known as Riboflavin, is an essential water-soluble vitamin that plays a crucial role in energy production and cellular function. It is particularly important in the dietary recommendations for infants, where it is advised to be administered in quantities of 3.6 mg according to daily vitamin recommendations."}{"title": "NIACINA:NIACINA, tambi\u00e9n conocida como vitamina B\u2083, es un nutriente esencial que desempe\u00f1a un papel crucial como coenzima en diversos procesos metab\u00f3licos. Esta vitamina soluble en agua es fundamental para la conversi\u00f3n de los alimentos en energ\u00eda y se incluye com\u00fanmente en la composici\u00f3n de multivitaminas para la nutrici\u00f3n parenteral. La niacina es importante no solo para el metabolismo energ\u00e9tico, sino tambi\u00e9n para la reparaci\u00f3n del ADN. Se encuentra en alimentos como la carne, las patatas y el pan. La deficiencia de niacina puede provocar s\u00edntomas que se asemejan a los del s\u00edndrome carcinoide. Seg\u00fan las recomendaciones diarias de vitaminas, se sugiere una ingesta de 40 mg de niacina."}{"title": "VITAMINA B6:VITAMINA B6, also known as Pyridoxine, is a water-soluble vitamin that plays a crucial role in various physiological processes. It is essential for protein metabolism, amino acid metabolism, and neurotransmitter synthesis, making it vital for brain development and function. The vitamin is included in nutritional guidelines for infants, highlighting its importance during early growth stages. \n\nDeficiency in Vitamin B6 can lead to health issues, such as hypomagnesemia, as it influences magnesium metabolism. Additionally, certain medications, like isoniazid, can contribute to Vitamin B6 deficiency. The recommended daily intake of Vitamin B6 is approximately 4 mg, and it is commonly found in foods such as meats, fish, eggs, and whole grains. For supplementation, Vitamin B6 is available in various forms, including Benad\u00f3n 300 mg, which can be administered in both tablet and injectable forms."}{"title": "VITAMINA B12:VITAMINA B12, also known as Cobalamin, is a crucial water-soluble vitamin that plays an essential role in various bodily functions, particularly in the formation of red blood cells and the maintenance of the nervous system. It is vital for nerve function and the production of DNA, and its deficiency can lead to significant health issues, including anemia and neurological problems.\n\nDeficiency in VITAMINA B12 is commonly observed in individuals with unbalanced diets, particularly among vegans, the elderly, and patients with certain medical conditions such as celiac disease, inflammatory bowel disease, and those who have undergone gastric bypass surgery. These groups may require supplementation to prevent deficiencies. Additionally, patients undergoing dialysis may also need VITAMINA B12 supplementation due to losses during treatment.\n\nVITAMINA B12 is typically monitored in patients with cystic fibrosis and those receiving parenteral nutrition, as absorption issues can arise in these populations. It is included in various multivitamin formulations, such as Infuvite Pedi\u00e1trico, to support overall health. The vitamin is found naturally in foods such as liver, eggs, milk, and fish, and specific intake recommendations exist to ensure adequate levels.\n\nDespite its importance, upper limits for VITAMINA B12 intake have not been established due to a lack of data on adverse effects. The recommended daily intake is approximately 5 micrograms. VITAMINA B12 works in conjunction with folate to help prevent elevated homocysteine levels, which are associated with various health risks. \n\nIn summary, VITAMINA B12 is an essential nutrient that requires careful monitoring and supplementation in certain populations to maintain optimal health and prevent deficiencies."}{"title": "PANTOT\u00c9NICO:Vitamina que debe ser administrada en cantidades de 15 mg seg\u00fan las recomendaciones diarias de vitaminas"}{"title": "VITAMINA C:Vitamin C, also known as Ascorbic Acid, is a water-soluble vitamin that plays a crucial role in various bodily functions. It is recognized for its antioxidant properties, which help protect cells from oxidative stress, and is essential for the growth and repair of tissues, including skin, bones, and connective tissue. Vitamin C acts as a cofactor for numerous enzymes and is involved in the conversion of dopamine to noradrenaline, contributing to brain health.\n\nThis vitamin is particularly important for enhancing the absorption of non-heme iron by reducing ferric (Fe3+) to ferrous (Fe2+) state, making it vital for individuals with iron deficiency. It is often recommended for patients with specific dietary conditions, such as those with glucose-galactose malabsorption or hereditary fructose intolerance, as it is found in foods that may be restricted for these individuals.\n\nIn clinical settings, Vitamin C supplementation may be necessary for patients with certain health conditions, including those undergoing cancer treatment, cirrhotic patients, and individuals with inflammatory bowel disease (EII). However, it is important to monitor intake to avoid exceeding recommended daily allowances, as excessive amounts can lead to increased urinary oxalate excretion and potentially contribute to kidney stone formation.\n\nVitamin C is sensitive to heat and storage conditions, which can degrade its nutritional quality. It is commonly included in multivitamin formulations for parenteral nutrition and is available in various supplement forms, such as \u00c1cido Asc\u00f3rbico Bayer and Redoxc. Overall, Vitamin C is an essential nutrient that supports immune function, skin health, and overall well-being, and its intake should be carefully managed, especially in critical patients."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO F\u00d3LICO:\u00c1cido F\u00f3lico, also known as folic acid, is a vital B vitamin that plays a crucial role in various metabolic functions and is particularly important for human health. It is essential for DNA and RNA synthesis, cell division, and the production of red blood cells. \u00c1cido F\u00f3lico is recommended for patients at risk of deficiency, including those undergoing nutritional therapy, individuals with celiac disease, and patients with eating disorders, as it can significantly affect their metabolic functions and recovery.\n\nThe recommended daily intake of \u00c1cido F\u00f3lico is 400 micrograms (\u03bcg), which is particularly emphasized for women who are planning to become pregnant, as it helps reduce the risk of neural tube defects in their offspring. Additionally, it is suggested that supplementation may be necessary for certain populations, such as older adults, patients with cystic fibrosis, and those undergoing treatments like methotrexate, which can lead to deficiencies.\n\n\u00c1cido F\u00f3lico is found in various foods, including leafy green vegetables, legumes, and organ meats. While some studies suggest that supplementation may not provide additional benefits beyond a standard multivitamin, it remains a critical nutrient for preventing megaloblastic anemia and supporting overall health. It is also noted for its potential protective effects against certain types of cancer and its role in reducing homocysteine levels, which can lower the risk of circulatory problems in the brain.\n\nIn summary, \u00c1cido F\u00f3lico is an essential B vitamin that supports metabolic health, particularly during pregnancy and in individuals at risk of deficiency, and is available in various supplement forms."}{"title": "BIOTINA:Biotina, also known as Vitamin H, is a water-soluble vitamin that plays a crucial role in fatty acid synthesis and energy metabolism. It is included in the multivitamin composition for parenteral nutrition, specifically in products like Infuvite Pedi\u00e1trico. Biotin supports metabolic functions and is beneficial for the health of hair, skin, and nails. Notably, there are no established upper limits for biotin intake due to a lack of data on adverse effects. According to daily vitamin recommendations, biotin should be administered in quantities of 60 micrograms."}{"title": "ZINC:Zinc is an essential trace element and micronutrient that plays a critical role in various bodily functions, including immune response, protein synthesis, wound healing, and cognitive development. It is particularly important for the growth and development of children and is often included in infant formulas to support immune function and overall health. The recommended daily intake of zinc varies by age and gender, with general guidelines suggesting a daily intake of 10-20 mg for adults and specific recommendations for pediatric patients.\n\nZinc deficiency is frequently observed in various health conditions, including chronic liver disease, cirrhosis, inflammatory bowel disease, and after biliopancreatic diversion surgeries. It is also common in patients with eating disorders, cystic fibrosis, and those undergoing parenteral nutrition. Deficiencies can lead to significant health issues, such as impaired wound healing, immune dysfunction, and alterations in taste perception. In critically ill patients, zinc supplementation is recommended to support recovery, and it is also suggested for children experiencing acute diarrhea, as per WHO and UNICEF guidelines.\n\nZinc is involved in numerous biological processes, including DNA replication and transcription, and it helps reduce infections, particularly in older adults. While zinc is crucial for health, excessive levels can contribute to oxidative stress and neurodegeneration. Therefore, monitoring zinc levels is important, especially in patients with specific health conditions or those at risk of deficiency. Zinc supplements are available in various forms, including capsules and tablets, to help individuals meet their nutritional needs."}{"title": "COBRE:Cobre, or copper, is a trace mineral that plays a crucial role in various physiological processes, including iron metabolism, the formation of red blood cells, and the development of connective tissue. It is an essential micronutrient that is particularly important for pediatric patients, with specific dosage recommendations ranging from 0.5 to 1.5 mg according to daily guidelines. Copper deficiency is common, especially after procedures like biliopancreatic diversion, and it often presents asymptomatically. Additionally, copper levels are routinely tested to assess nutritional status and identify potential deficiencies in individuals, particularly those with eating disorders. In summary, cobre is vital for growth, bone mineralization, and the production of red blood cells, highlighting its importance in maintaining overall health."}{"title": "CROMO:CROMO, also known as chromium, is a trace element that plays a significant role in glucose and lipid metabolism. It is recognized as a micronutrient that may improve glycemic control and insulin resistance, particularly in diabetic patients and those at risk. Chromium is found in various foods, including meat and potatoes, and its dietary reference intake varies by age and gender, with specific recommended daily intake levels established.\n\nDespite its benefits, caution is advised regarding chromium supplementation, as upper limits for intake have not been established due to insufficient data on potential adverse effects. There are concerns about its nephrotoxicity in neonates, necessitating careful administration in pediatric parenteral nutrition. Generally, supplementation is not deemed necessary for most individuals, as chromium can be adequately obtained through a balanced diet. The recommended intake for chromium is typically between 0.01 to 0.02 mg, according to daily guidelines for trace elements."}{"title": "MANGANESO:Manganeso, o mangan\u00e9s, es un micronutriente esencial y un oligoelemento que desempe\u00f1a un papel crucial en el metabolismo, la formaci\u00f3n de huesos, la coagulaci\u00f3n sangu\u00ednea y la reducci\u00f3n de la inflamaci\u00f3n. Su deficiencia, aunque poco com\u00fan, puede tener implicaciones cl\u00ednicas significativas, especialmente en pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal. Este mineral se encuentra en alimentos como el arroz y los frutos secos, y est\u00e1 vinculado a la acci\u00f3n antioxidante.\n\nEs importante tener en cuenta que, aunque el manganeso es esencial para la salud, su administraci\u00f3n en dosis elevadas puede resultar t\u00f3xica, afectando negativamente al h\u00edgado y al sistema nervioso central. Por lo tanto, se recomienda un consumo controlado, con niveles de ingesta diaria sugeridos que oscilan entre 0.15 y 0.8 mg, especialmente en pacientes pedi\u00e1tricos y en ciertas condiciones m\u00e9dicas. En resumen, el manganeso es un mineral vital que contribuye a diversas funciones biol\u00f3gicas, pero debe ser consumido con precauci\u00f3n para evitar efectos adversos."}{"title": "COBALTO:Cobalto, also known as cobalt, is a trace element that plays a crucial role in the formation of vitamin B12, which is essential for the production of red blood cells. It is important to administer cobalt in specific dosages, typically ranging from 0.002 to 0.005 mg, in accordance with daily recommendations for trace elements."}{"title": "SODIO:Sodio, or sodium, is an essential electrolyte that plays a critical role in maintaining fluid balance and is vital for proper muscle and nerve function. It is necessary for various bodily functions, including hydration, especially during exercise, and is crucial in the nutrition of newborns to prevent complications. In pediatric nutrition, specific daily requirements for sodium must be adhered to, particularly for patients receiving parenteral nutrition, where sodium levels need to be monitored and supplemented appropriately.\n\nSodio is also significant in dietary contexts, as it helps regulate the balance of fluids in the body and can affect the reabsorption of lithium in the kidneys. However, excessive sodium intake is associated with health issues such as hypertension and cardiovascular problems, leading to recommendations for limiting sodium consumption. Dietary guidelines suggest that sodium intake should be restricted to below 3.5 g/day to reduce the risk of kidney stones and manage blood pressure, particularly in individuals with diabetes or fluid retention.\n\nSodio is present in various foods, including Galleta Maria, where it contributes to flavor and preservation. It is important to note that sodium levels can be affected in patients with conditions like renal insufficiency, cor pulmonale, and respiratory failure, necessitating careful management of sodium intake. Normal sodium levels in the body typically range between 135 and 145 mEq/l, and its interaction with other minerals, such as magnesium, further underscores the need for balanced dietary intake. Overall, while sodium is a crucial nutrient, its consumption must be carefully managed to promote health and prevent complications."}{"title": "SELENIO:SELENIO, or selenium, is an essential trace mineral and micronutrient that plays a critical role in various bodily functions, particularly in antioxidant defense and thyroid function. It is recommended as a supplement for patients, with a suggested daily intake of 100 mg, although specific dosage recommendations may vary based on factors such as age and gender. Selenium is known for its antioxidant properties, which help protect against free radicals, and it is a cofactor for the enzyme glutathione peroxidase, crucial for maintaining cellular health.\n\nDeficiency in selenium has been associated with several health issues, including coronary pathology, immunosuppression, and certain neoplasias. In particular, its deficiency can lead to reversible myocardiopathy and irreversible encephalitis in patients with inflammatory bowel disease. Additionally, selenium deficiency is linked to the development of goiter due to its role in thyroid hormone synthesis. While selenium is generally rare in deficiency, it can be particularly low in patients with chronic liver disease, those undergoing prolonged dialysis, and individuals who have had certain surgeries.\n\nSelenium supplementation is advised with caution, especially in patients with renal insufficiency, and its use in oncology is not sufficiently supported by evidence. It has been suggested as a protective factor against cardiovascular diseases and cancer due to its anti-inflammatory and antioxidant properties. Regular monitoring of selenium levels in the blood is recommended for individuals on restricted diets or those not supplementing regularly. Overall, selenium is a vital micronutrient that contributes significantly to metabolic processes and immune health."}{"title": "YODO:YODO, or iodine, is an essential trace element crucial for the production of thyroid hormones, which play a significant role in regulating metabolism and overall health. It is particularly important for growth and development, especially in children. A deficiency in iodine is the most common cause of hypothyroidism worldwide. \n\nIodine is found in various dietary sources, notably seafood and iodized salt, and its intake has improved in countries like Spain. However, health authorities recommend universal consumption of iodized salt, particularly for vulnerable populations such as pregnant and lactating women. \n\nThe recommended daily intake of iodine varies by age and gender, highlighting its importance in maintaining proper thyroid function and metabolic processes. Additionally, iodine is utilized in diagnostic studies and treatments related to thyroid health. Overall, YODO is a vital nutrient that supports thyroid hormone synthesis and contributes to metabolic regulation."}{"title": "HIERRO:HIERRO, or iron, is an essential mineral that plays a critical role in various biological processes, particularly in the production of hemoglobin, which is responsible for transporting oxygen in the blood. It is vital for maintaining healthy blood production and is necessary for energy metabolism, especially in athletes. Iron is also important for DNA synthesis and cognitive development in early childhood.\n\nWhile iron deficiency is not common in the geriatric population, it is crucial to monitor iron levels in patients with renal insufficiency to prevent anemia and ensure the effectiveness of treatments like erythropoietin. In cases of iron deficiency anemia, iron supplementation is necessary, but it should be prescribed carefully and monitored to avoid excessive iron intake, which can lead to serious health issues such as hemochromatosis.\n\nIron is included in infant formulas to prevent iron deficiency anemia, particularly in preterm infants, and is provided in specific dosages. For infants and children receiving parenteral nutrition for extended periods, iron supplementation is recommended. However, the addition of iron to infant nutrition is controversial, especially for preterm infants.\n\nIn terms of dietary intake, the normal recommended levels for healthy individuals range from 10-20 mg daily, with specific intake recommendations varying based on age and gender. Iron is absorbed in its ferrous state and can form insoluble complexes with certain medications, affecting their bioavailability. It is also essential for patients with conditions like cystic fibrosis and inflammatory bowel disease, where deficiencies can contribute to anemia.\n\nOverall, HIERRO is a vital micronutrient that must be managed carefully to support health and prevent deficiencies across different populations, including the elderly, infants, and those with specific health conditions."}{"title": "NUTRICIONES COMERCIALIZADAS:Commercial nutrition formulations are ready-to-use mixtures produced by the pharmaceutical industry, containing macronutrients but lacking vitamins and trace elements."}{"title": "ADMINISTRACI\u00d3N DE NP:The administration of parenteral nutrition (NP) involves specific protocols to ensure patient safety and effective nutrient delivery through central venous access."}{"title": "TRAUMATISMO CRANEOENCEF\u00c1LICO SEVERO:Severe cranioencephalic trauma is a critical medical condition that can lead to increased urinary losses of zinc, necessitating higher supplementation."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA HEP\u00c1TICA:Insuficiencia hep\u00e1tica, or hepatic insufficiency, is a severe medical condition characterized by the liver's inability to perform its normal functions. This condition necessitates urgent medical care and careful management of various dietary factors. Specifically, individuals with hepatic insufficiency require specific dietary adjustments, including limited intake of copper and manganese, as well as careful management of lipid intake, particularly in cases involving parenteral nutrition. Furthermore, this condition can significantly impact the metabolism of nutrients, especially in newborns, highlighting the critical nature of liver function in overall nutritional status and metabolic processes."}{"title": "COLSTASIS:COLSTASIS is a medical condition characterized by reduced bile flow, which can lead to various complications. This condition necessitates dietary modifications, specifically limiting the intake of copper and manganese to manage its effects. Additionally, cholestasis can occur in patients who are receiving prolonged parenteral nutrition, where the flow of bile is either reduced or completely blocked."}{"title": "TIAMINA:TIAMINA, also known as Thiamine or Vitamin B1, is a water-soluble vitamin that plays a crucial role in energy metabolism, particularly in the conversion of carbohydrates into energy. It is included in parenteral nutrition formulations, such as Infuvite Pedi\u00e1trico, to support metabolic processes and prevent complications in patients at risk during the first week of nutritional therapy. Thiamine is essential for nerve function and is found in various food sources, including cereals, potatoes, and pork.\n\nDeficiency in Thiamine can lead to serious health issues, such as Wernicke's encephalopathy, particularly in patients who have undergone certain surgeries or those with alcohol-related liver disease. Additionally, patients on dialysis may require increased intake of Thiamine. While it is sometimes considered for supplementation in patients with cognitive decline, the benefits of such supplementation remain debated. Thiamine is also recommended as a supplement for all forms of Maple Syrup Urine Disease to improve patient outcomes. Notably, there are no established upper limits for Thiamine intake due to a lack of data on adverse effects. Overall, Thiamine is a vital nutrient that is part of the B-complex vitamins and is critical for maintaining energy metabolism and overall health."}{"title": "ENFERMEDADES CR\u00d3NICAS:\"ENFERMEDADES CR\u00d3NICAS\" refers to long-term health conditions that significantly impact an individual's nutritional status and overall health. These chronic diseases, which include diabetes, obesity, cardiovascular diseases, and cancer, are major contributors to mortality and disability on a global scale. They are often associated with lifestyle and dietary factors, highlighting the importance of nutrition in their management. In particular, chronic diseases can lead to complications such as chronic kidney disease and phosphorus imbalance. Additionally, pediatric patients with chronic diseases may require specialized nutritional support and management to address their unique health needs. Overall, \"ENFERMEDADES CR\u00d3NICAS\" encompasses a range of health issues that necessitate careful consideration of dietary habits and nutritional interventions."}{"title": "ALCOHOLISMO:Alcoholism, known as \"alcoholismo\" in Spanish, is a chronic disease characterized by an inability to control or stop drinking despite experiencing negative consequences. This condition can lead to various health issues, including nutritional deficiencies and liver diseases such as cirrhosis. Additionally, alcoholism can result in decreased magnesium absorption, contributing to hypomagnesemia, and may cause physiological hypercortisolism. It is also noted that alcoholism can be a contraindication for the use of very low-calorie diets (VLCD). The biochemical alterations associated with alcoholism can improve with abstinence from alcohol, highlighting the potential for recovery and health restoration."}{"title": "DROGADICCI\u00d3N:Drogadicci\u00f3n refers to the compulsive use of drugs, which can severely impact a person's nutritional health and overall well-being."}{"title": "ALTO GRADO DE ESTR\u00c9S METAB\u00d3LICO:Alto grado de estr\u00e9s metab\u00f3lico refers to a condition where the body's metabolic demands are significantly increased, often requiring careful nutritional management."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROMES DE MALA ABSORCI\u00d3N:S\u00edndromes de mala absorci\u00f3n are conditions that prevent the body from properly absorbing nutrients from food, leading to malnutrition."}{"title": "ANOREXIA NERVIOSA:Anorexia Nervosa (AN) is a serious eating disorder characterized by an intense fear of gaining weight and a distorted body image. This condition leads to self-imposed starvation, excessive weight loss, and restricted energy intake, resulting in significantly low body weight. Individuals with anorexia nervosa often engage in behaviors that interfere with weight gain, even when they are severely underweight. The disorder can cause severe health complications, including malnutrition, osteoporosis, hormonal imbalances, and primary amenorrhea in prepubertal patients. \n\nAnorexia nervosa raises complex medical and ethical issues, particularly regarding treatment and patient autonomy, especially in detention settings. It can lead to severe health risks, necessitating nutritional rehabilitation and, in some cases, enteral nutrition support. The disorder is also associated with physiological conditions such as hypercortisolism, although it rarely presents with clinical features of Cushing's syndrome. Overall, anorexia nervosa is a multifaceted mental health disorder that poses significant challenges for both patients and healthcare providers."}{"title": "DENSITOMETR\u00cdA \u00d3SEA:DENSITOMETR\u00cdA \u00d3SEA refers to bone densitometry, a specialized test that measures bone density. This assessment is crucial for evaluating the risk of osteoporosis, particularly in individuals undergoing hormone therapy. Additionally, bone densitometry is utilized to assess the risk of fractures and overall bone health, which can be adversely affected in patients with eating disorders. The procedure is also significant in the context of parenteral nutrition, as it helps evaluate the patient's bone health in relation to their nutritional status. Overall, DENSITOMETR\u00cdA \u00d3SEA plays a vital role in monitoring and managing bone health across various patient populations."}{"title": "CONTROL ANAL\u00cdTICO:El control anal\u00edtico es un proceso de evaluaci\u00f3n del estado metab\u00f3lico y nutricional del paciente durante el tratamiento de nutrici\u00f3n parenteral."}{"title": "SEGUIMIENTO:SEGUIMIENTO refers to the continuous process of monitoring and evaluating a patient's health status, particularly in the context of assessing the effectiveness of parenteral nutrition and preventing complications. This ongoing medical supervision involves regular assessments to ensure that the patient's treatment is effective and to identify any necessary adjustments. Additionally, SEGUIMIENTO encompasses the monitoring of production processes to ensure that products meet quality standards. Overall, SEGUIMIENTO is a comprehensive approach that integrates patient health monitoring with quality assurance in medical treatments."}{"title": "TEMPERATURA CORPORAL:La temperatura corporal se mide para detectar complicaciones infecciosas en el paciente que recibe nutrici\u00f3n parenteral."}{"title": "CONTROL F\u00cdSICO:El control f\u00edsico implica detectar carencias nutricionales y evaluar el estado de hidrataci\u00f3n del paciente durante la nutrici\u00f3n parenteral."}{"title": "ESTADO FUNCIONAL:El estado funcional se eval\u00faa mediante la fuerza del brazo y la resistencia f\u00edsica del paciente durante el tratamiento de nutrici\u00f3n parenteral."}{"title": "FUNCION GASTROINTESTINAL:La funci\u00f3n gastrointestinal se controla para detectar alteraciones en la ingesta del paciente que recibe nutrici\u00f3n parenteral."}{"title": "FUNCION CARDIO-RESPIRATORIA:"}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARI I POLIT\u00c8CNIC:Hospital Universitari i Polit\u00e8cnic is a healthcare institution involved in the provision of specialized nutritional support and parenteral nutrition protocols."}{"title": "NUTRICIONES PARENTERALES ADULTOS PROTOCOLIZADAS EN EL HOSPITAL:A protocol for adult parenteral nutrition established in the hospital, detailing the nutritional components and monitoring processes."}{"title": "SEFH:SEFH is the Spanish Society of Hospital Pharmacy, which collaborates on the preparation of parenteral nutrition mixtures."}{"title": "GLUTAMINE AND ANTIOXIDANTS TRIAL:A randomized trial assessing the effects of glutamine and antioxidants in critically ill patients, published in the New England Journal of Medicine."}{"title": "GUIDELINES FOR THE USE OF PARENTERAL AND ENTERAL NUTRITION:A set of guidelines published for the use of parenteral and enteral nutrition in adult and pediatric patients."}{"title": "STANDARDS FOR NUTRITION SUPPORT:Standards established for nutrition support in hospitalized adult patients, detailing best practices in clinical nutrition."}{"title": "BIBLIOGRAFIA:BIBLIOGRAFIA refers to the list of sources and references cited in a document. It serves to provide evidence and support for the information presented, as well as the guidelines discussed. This compilation of references is essential for validating the content and ensuring the credibility of the work."}{"title": "CER-NEVIT:CER-NEVIT is a multivitamin composition used in parenteral nutrition for adults, containing various vitamins and excipients."}{"title": "A. NAVARRO EDUARDO:A. Navarro Eduardo is an author contributing to the chapter on access routes in parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "V\u00cdA PERIF\u00c9RICA:V\u00cdA PERIF\u00c9RICA refers to a method of venous access utilized in parenteral nutrition, specifically designed for situations where the osmolarity of the nutritional solution is below 800 mOsm/l. This method involves administering nutrition through peripheral veins, making it a suitable option when central venous access is not available."}{"title": "VITAMINA D3:Vitamin D3, also known as Cholecalciferol or colecalciferol, is a fat-soluble vitamin that plays a crucial role in regulating calcium and phosphate levels in the body. It is essential for maintaining bone health and supporting immune function. Vitamin D3 is produced in the skin in response to sunlight and is included in the multivitamin composition for parenteral nutrition. It is recognized as a more effective form of vitamin D compared to D2 in raising vitamin D levels in the body. Additionally, it is noted that some patients may be deficient in Vitamin D3, highlighting its importance for overall health."}{"title": "RIBOFLAVINA:Riboflavin, also known as Vitamin B2, is a water-soluble vitamin that plays a crucial role in energy production and cellular function. It is an essential component of the B-complex vitamins and is included in parenteral nutrition formulations, such as Infuvite Pedi\u00e1trico, to support overall health. Riboflavin is recognized for its importance in energy metabolism, and it is included in the multivitamin composition for parenteral nutrition. Notably, there are currently no established upper limits for riboflavin intake due to insufficient data on potential adverse effects."}{"title": "PIRIDOXINA:Pyridoxina, commonly known as Vitamin B6, is a water-soluble vitamin that plays a crucial role in various physiological processes. It is involved in amino acid metabolism and neurotransmitter synthesis, making it important for cognitive development and overall brain health. While there is some discussion regarding its potential benefits for cognitive health and dementia, the evidence supporting its effectiveness in these areas is limited.\n\nPyridoxina is also included in parenteral nutrition formulations, highlighting its significance in protein metabolism. It is a key component of multivitamin compositions used in parenteral nutrition, such as Infuvite Pedi\u00e1trico, ensuring that individuals receiving this form of nutrition obtain essential nutrients for their health. Overall, Pyridoxina is recognized for its vital contributions to metabolic processes and its inclusion in nutritional support therapies."}{"title": "AC. F\u00d3LICO:Folic acid is a B-vitamin important for cell division and the production of DNA, included in the multivitamin composition for parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "AC. DEXPANTOT\u00c9NICO:Dexpanthenol (Vitamin B5) is a water-soluble vitamin involved in the synthesis of coenzyme A, included in the multivitamin composition for parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "HICKMAN:Hickman is a type of tunneled central venous catheter designed for accessing the venous system, particularly beneficial for patients requiring long-term intravenous therapy, such as those undergoing oncology treatments and other medical interventions. This catheter is known for its lower infection rates compared to non-tunneled catheters, making it a preferred choice for sustained venous access."}{"title": "PORT-A-CATH:Port-a-Cath is a brand of totally implanted catheter designed for long-term access to the vascular system, primarily for patients who require frequent blood draws or infusions. It is classified as a type of central venous catheter, which necessitates regular maintenance, including sealing every 1 to 6 months to prevent thrombotic obstruction. This device provides a reliable solution for patients needing ongoing vascular access."}{"title": "SOLDINGHER:Seldingher is a technique used for the puncture of large veins, such as the internal jugular or subclavian veins, for catheter insertion."}{"title": "UCIS ESPA\u00d1OLAS:UCIs Espa\u00f1olas refers to Intensive Care Units in Spain, which follow specific protocols for preventing infections related to catheter use."}{"title": "VENAS:Veins are blood vessels that are accessed for catheter insertion, including antecubital, jugular, subclavian, and femoral veins."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N PARENTERAL:ALIMENTACI\u00d3N PARENTERAL es un m\u00e9todo de nutrici\u00f3n que se administra por v\u00eda intravenosa. Este tratamiento se utiliza en pacientes que no pueden recibir alimentos por v\u00eda oral o enteral, proporcionando as\u00ed la nutrici\u00f3n necesaria de manera efectiva."}{"title": "CATAETERES:Catheters are medical devices used to deliver fluids or medications directly into the bloodstream or to drain fluids from the body."}{"title": "NEUMOT\u00d3RAX:NEUMOT\u00d3RAX is a medical condition characterized by the presence of air in the pleural space, which is the area between the lung and the chest wall. This condition can arise as a complication during various medical procedures, particularly during the insertion of a central venous catheter. The risk of developing a pneumothorax is notably associated with central parenteral nutrition and other venous access procedures, where improper technique or accidental puncture of the pleura may lead to air leakage. Overall, pneumothorax is a significant concern in clinical settings, as it can complicate patient care and necessitate further medical intervention."}{"title": "HEMOT\u00d3RAX:Hemot\u00f3rax is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of blood in the pleural cavity. This condition can arise as a complication during the insertion of a catheter, particularly due to arterial puncture. Hemot\u00f3rax represents a significant risk associated with catheter procedures, highlighting the importance of careful technique to prevent such complications."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA:\"NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA\" (NPD) refers to home parenteral nutrition, a medical treatment designed for patients who are unable to receive adequate nutrition through oral intake. This form of home nutritional therapy involves the intravenous delivery of essential nutrients directly into the bloodstream, making it a vital option for individuals with conditions such as intestinal failure or other gastrointestinal disorders that prevent normal food consumption.\n\nNPD allows stable patients to receive nutritional support in the comfort of their own homes, significantly improving their quality of life while reducing the risk of hospital-related complications. It is particularly beneficial for those requiring long-term nutritional therapy, as it provides a means to maintain nutritional status outside of a clinical setting.\n\nThe method has been analyzed for its cost-effectiveness compared to traditional hospital-based nutrition, and it is documented annually by the NADYA group, which tracks the health implications and associated costs of home parenteral nutrition. Overall, \"NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA\" serves as a crucial intervention for patients who cannot meet their nutritional needs through natural food sources, facilitating their rehabilitation and enhancing their overall well-being."}{"title": "A. SEGURA:A. Segura is one of the authors discussing complications related to parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "YUGULAR VEIN:The jugular vein is a central venous access site with a low risk in the technique for catheter insertion."}{"title": "FEMORAL VEIN:The femoral vein is a central venous access site that is easy to access but has a higher risk of infection."}{"title": "CATHETER-RELATED BLOODSTREAM INFECTION:Catheter-related bloodstream infection is a serious complication associated with the use of central venous catheters."}{"title": "SUBCLAVIA VEIN:"}{"title": "STAPHYLOCOCCUS:Staphylococcus is a genus of bacteria, with S.epidermidis and S.aureus being the most common types associated with catheter infections."}{"title": "KLEBSIELLA:Klebsiella is a type of gram-negative bacteria known to cause infections, particularly in patients who have catheters or those who are immunocompromised. This bacterium poses a significant risk in healthcare settings, where it can lead to serious infections."}{"title": "CANDIDA ALBICANS:Candida albicans is a type of fungus that can lead to infections, particularly in patients with catheters and those who are immunocompromised. It is known to cause various infections and has been mentioned as a potential cause of diarrhea in certain patients. This opportunistic pathogen poses a significant risk, especially in vulnerable populations, highlighting the importance of monitoring and managing infections associated with this fungus."}{"title": "BATERIEMIA 0:Bacteriemia 0 is a hospital protocol aimed at preventing infections during catheter placement and manipulation."}{"title": "SYNDROME DE REALIMENTACION:The syndrome of realimentation occurs in severely malnourished patients undergoing intensive nutritional replenishment, leading to various metabolic complications."}{"title": "INSULINA:Insulina is a crucial hormone produced by the pancreas that plays a significant role in regulating blood glucose levels and is essential in the management of diabetes, particularly Type 1 diabetes. It is administered to patients in various regimens to control hyperglycemia and prevent complications such as ketoacidosis. Insulin therapy is a vital component of diabetes management, especially for critically ill patients, as it helps maintain blood glucose levels near normal and influences overall metabolic processes.\n\nIn the context of diabetes treatment, insulin is often used when other medications are insufficient. It is particularly important for managing blood sugar levels during acute conditions, such as diabetic ketoacidosis and in patients with hyperglycemia due to acute pancreatitis. Insulin administration can also affect nutritional status and health in patients with conditions like pancreatic cancer and cirrhosis.\n\nPatients may require adjustments to their insulin dosages based on their individual needs, and monitoring is essential to ensure effective management of their blood glucose levels. Insulin can also be included in parenteral nutrition protocols when necessary. However, some patients may struggle with adherence to their insulin regimen, leading to omitted doses, which can complicate their diabetes management.\n\nOverall, insulin is a fundamental medication in the treatment of diabetes, helping to regulate glucose metabolism and maintain health in individuals with this chronic condition."}{"title": "HIPERGLUCEMIA:HIPERGLUCEMIA is a medical condition characterized by elevated blood glucose levels. This condition can occur in various patient populations, particularly in those receiving nutritional therapy, such as enteral and parenteral nutrition. It is commonly seen in diabetic patients, critically ill individuals, and those undergoing surgical procedures, as well as in newborns with very low birth weight due to excessive glucose intake.\n\nIn patients receiving parenteral nutrition, hyperglycemia is a frequent complication that arises when nutrient intake exceeds the body's metabolic clearance capacity. It can also complicate the diagnosis of other conditions, such as hyponatremia, and is notably prevalent in patients suffering from pancreatitis, where blood glucose levels can become abnormally high. Additionally, hyperglycemia can affect recovery in surgical patients and is a concern in the management of critically ill patients.\n\nThe condition is also associated with the use of steroids in transplant patients, which can contribute to elevated blood glucose levels. Overall, hyperglycemia is a significant metabolic complication that requires careful monitoring and management in various clinical settings."}{"title": "HIPOGLUCEMIA:Hipo glucemia, also known as hypoglycemia, is a medical condition characterized by abnormally low levels of glucose in the blood. This condition is commonly observed in patients with various underlying health issues, including Glycogen Storage Disease type III (GSDIII), diabetes, insulinomas, and urea cycle disorders. \n\nIn individuals with diabetes, particularly those undergoing insulin therapy or certain medications, the risk of hypoglycemia is heightened. It can also occur in patients receiving enteral nutrition, often linked to inadequate nutritional intake or excessive diabetic treatment. Additionally, hypoglycemia may manifest in hospitalized patients, especially those on insulin, and can be a concern in the dietary management of patients with specific metabolic disorders.\n\nHypoglycemia can lead to serious health issues if not treated promptly, with symptoms that may include confusion and weakness. It is also noted that this condition can arise from prolonged fasting, as seen in patients with fructose-1,6-bisphosphate deficiency, and may be associated with the treatment of hyperglycemia. In newborns, particularly those with restricted nutritional supply, hypoglycemia can occur due to insufficient glucose availability.\n\nFurthermore, hypoglycemia is recognized as a potential side effect of growth hormone treatment and can stimulate the secretion of growth hormone itself. In some cases, it may also be linked to acute hyponatremia, which is a medical emergency that can lead to severe complications such as cerebral edema.\n\nOverall, hypoglycemia is a multifaceted condition that requires careful management to prevent adverse health outcomes."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES HIDROELECTROL\u00cdTICAS:ALTERACIONES HIDROELECTROL\u00cdTICAS refer to disturbances in the levels of electrolytes in the body, which can lead to serious health issues, particularly in malnourished patients. These imbalances often necessitate careful monitoring and management to prevent complications and ensure the well-being of affected individuals."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARI I POLIT\u00c8CNIC LA FE:Hospital Universitari i Polit\u00e8cnic La Fe is a comprehensive medical facility that offers a wide range of healthcare services. It specializes in providing nutritional support for patients, especially in surgical contexts, ensuring that their dietary needs are met during recovery. Additionally, the hospital is actively involved in the treatment and management of patients suffering from acute pancreatitis, highlighting its commitment to addressing complex medical conditions."}{"title": "F. MINGOL NAVARRO:F. Mingol Navarro is a medical professional and co-author who focuses on the nutritional needs of surgical patients. He is actively involved in both the study and practice of nutritional support, emphasizing the importance of addressing these needs to improve patient outcomes in surgical settings."}{"title": "M. SAUR\u00cd ORTIZ:M. Saur\u00ed Ortiz is a medical professional and co-author who focuses on the nutritional needs of surgical patients. He collaborates on research and practices that emphasize the importance of nutritional support in this patient population, contributing valuable insights to the field."}{"title": "HIPERTRIGLICERIDEMIA:Hipertrigliceridemia, also known as hypertriglyceridemia, is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of triglycerides in the blood. This condition can arise from various causes, including genetic disorders and acquired conditions. It is particularly concerning for patients with Glycogen Storage Disease I, as well as those receiving parenteral nutrition, where excessive lipid administration can lead to elevated triglyceride levels. \n\nManagement of hipertrigliceridemia often involves dietary adjustments to help control triglyceride levels. In patients on parenteral nutrition, careful monitoring is essential, as excessive lipid intake can exceed the body's ability to clear triglycerides, potentially leading to complications such as pancreatitis and pseudohyponatremia. Overall, hipertrigliceridemia is a significant health concern that requires attention to dietary management and monitoring, especially in vulnerable patient populations."}{"title": "HEPATOPAT\u00cdA:HEPATOPAT\u00cdA refers to a range of liver diseases characterized by liver dysfunction, which can lead to various complications such as hepatic encephalopathy, cirrhosis, and nutritional deficiencies. This condition may necessitate dietary modifications to support liver function and manage protein intake, particularly in patients receiving home parenteral nutrition or those with intestinal failure. Hepatopathy can arise from multiple factors, including excessive glucose or lipid administration, especially in individuals on long-term parenteral nutrition.\n\nAdditionally, hepatopathy is associated with metabolic disorders, such as Adrenoleukodystrophy and Wilson's disease, and can be a contraindication for certain weight loss medications. It is important to note that hepatopathy can affect the body's metabolism and may require specific dietary management, including considerations for ketogenic diets. Overall, hepatopathy encompasses any disease of the liver that impacts its function and structure, necessitating careful monitoring and treatment to prevent further complications."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD METAB\u00d3LICA \u00d3SEA:\"ENFERMEDAD METAB\u00d3LICA \u00d3SEA\" refers to a condition affecting bone metabolism, particularly prevalent in patients receiving long-term parenteral nutrition. This condition is characterized by osteoporosis and osteomalacia, leading to symptoms such as bone pain and an increased risk of fractures due to nutrient deficiencies. It encompasses various bone metabolic disorders that arise as a result of prolonged nutritional support via parenteral means."}{"title": "SURGICAL PATIENT:Surgical patients are individuals undergoing surgery who may require nutritional assessment and support."}{"title": "HARRIS AND BENEDICT FORMULA:The Harris and Benedict formula is used to calculate the energy requirements of patients."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL SUPPLEMENTATION:Nutritional supplementation encompasses the provision of additional nutrients to individuals, particularly in clinical settings, to enhance their nutritional status and meet dietary requirements. This practice is especially crucial for malnourished patients and those with specific health conditions, such as chronic diseases like Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD), liver disease, and during treatments like chemotherapy. \n\nNutritional supplementation can be administered either parenterally or enterally and is often employed to prepare patients for surgery, such as those undergoing procedures for gastric cancer. It plays a significant role in improving health outcomes, particularly in elderly individuals, by enhancing the effects of exercise, preventing frailty, and potentially improving cognitive function. \n\nThe use of dietary supplements, which may include vitamins, minerals, and other nutrients, is vital for supporting health in various patient populations, including those with conditions like dementia and cancer. Overall, nutritional supplementation is a critical component of patient care aimed at optimizing health and recovery in individuals with diverse nutritional needs."}{"title": "POSTOPERATIVE NUTRITION:Postoperative nutrition involves protocols to ensure oral intake and may include artificial nutrition if necessary."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT PREOPERATIVE:Nutritional support in the preoperative phase aims to maintain or improve the nutritional status before surgery."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT POSTOPERATIVE:Nutritional support in the postoperative phase focuses on ensuring adequate intake to promote recovery."}{"title": "MORBIMORTALIDAD PERIOPERATORIA:Morbimortalidad perioperatoria refers to the complications and mortality associated with surgical procedures."}{"title": "SNG:SNG, or Sonda Nasog\u00e1strica, is a medical device known as a nasogastric tube that is primarily used to provide nutritional support to patients who are unable to eat by mouth. This tube is utilized for enteral feeding, allowing for the administration of nutrition and medications directly to the stomach. It is particularly beneficial for patients with swallowing difficulties or those in poor general health who cannot undergo more invasive feeding interventions. The SNG serves as a critical tool in medical procedures, facilitating the delivery of air or water to the stomach as needed. Overall, SNG is an essential method for ensuring that patients receive the necessary nutrition when oral intake is not possible or safe."}{"title": "POLITRAUMATIZADO:El politraumatizado es un paciente que presenta m\u00faltiples lesiones y puede requerir soporte nutricional debido a sus necesidades energ\u00e9ticas aumentadas."}{"title": "NEOPLASIA DE ES\u00d3FAGO:La neoplasia de es\u00f3fago es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica que afecta la capacidad de un paciente para ingerir alimentos, lo que puede requerir atenci\u00f3n nutricional especial. Esta condici\u00f3n puede restringir anat\u00f3micamente el aparato digestivo, lo que indica la necesidad de nutrici\u00f3n enteral para asegurar que el paciente reciba los nutrientes necesarios."}{"title": "DIFICULTAD PARA LA INGESTA:La dificultad para la ingesta es una condici\u00f3n que puede llevar a la necesidad de nutrici\u00f3n enteral cuando un paciente no puede consumir alimentos por v\u00eda oral."}{"title": "CIRUG\u00cdA:CIRUG\u00cdA refers to surgical procedures that encompass a range of medical interventions, particularly significant in the context of patient care and recovery. These procedures often necessitate nutritional support, as they can lead to alterations in the nutritional status of patients, especially those with cancer, resulting in weight loss and potential complications. The surgical department is responsible for the comprehensive care and treatment of patients, which includes the administration of parenteral nutrition and the placement of enteral feeding tubes to ensure adequate nutritional intake.\n\nMoreover, surgery can impact critical health markers such as albumin levels and overall nutritional status, particularly in critically ill patients. It is also noted that surgical procedures may induce insulin resistance and hyperglycemia, which can further complicate recovery and affect patient outcomes. In specific cases, such as surgeries involving head and neck cancer patients, immunomodulatory formulas may be utilized to support recovery. Therefore, careful nutritional considerations are essential both before and after surgical interventions to optimize patient health and recovery outcomes."}{"title": "MALNUTRICI\u00d3N SEVERA:MALNUTRICI\u00d3N SEVERA es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica que puede se\u00f1alar la necesidad de iniciar nutrici\u00f3n enteral o parenteral con el fin de restaurar el estado nutricional del paciente."}{"title": "CIRUG\u00cdA ABDOMINAL:La cirug\u00eda abdominal es un procedimiento quir\u00fargico que puede requerir soporte nutricional, especialmente en pacientes desnutridos."}{"title": "PACIENTES DESNUTRIDOS:\"Pacientes Desnutridos\" refers to individuals suffering from malnutrition, who are at an increased risk of developing complications such as S\u00edndrome de Realimentaci\u00f3n when receiving nutritional support. These patients may require enteral nutrition before major surgeries or transplants, as well as parenteral or enteral nutrition both before and after surgical procedures. Malnourished patients are particularly vulnerable to health issues like hypophosphatemia, which can arise from their nutritional deficiencies. Often, this state of malnutrition is a consequence of eating disorders, highlighting the complex interplay between nutritional health and psychological factors."}{"title": "HIPOEMESIS GRAV\u00cdDICA:La hiper\u00e9mesis grav\u00eddica es una condici\u00f3n que puede causar desnutrici\u00f3n en mujeres embarazadas, requiriendo atenci\u00f3n nutricional especial."}{"title": "TRAUMATISMO PENETRANTE:El traumatismo penetrante es una lesi\u00f3n grave que puede requerir soporte nutricional en pacientes con un \u00edndice de gravedad elevado."}{"title": "TRAUMATISMO ABDOMINAL:El traumatismo abdominal es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica que puede llevar a la necesidad de nutrici\u00f3n parenteral en pacientes gravemente heridos."}{"title": "F\u00cdSTULAS ENTERO-CUT\u00c1NEAS:Las f\u00edstulas entero-cut\u00e1neas son complicaciones que pueden surgir en pacientes con problemas digestivos, afectando la nutrici\u00f3n y el tratamiento."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS INMUNOMODULADORAS:F\u00d3RMULAS INMUNOMODULADORAS are specialized enteral nutrition formulas designed to provide nutritional support for patients in various critical conditions, such as those undergoing cancer surgery or experiencing trauma. These immunomodulatory formulas contain specific nutrients aimed at influencing disease processes and enhancing the nutritional status of the patient. While they may offer benefits to certain critical patients, their use is not routine in clinical practice."}{"title": "NEOPLASIA G\u00c1STRICA:Neoplasia g\u00e1strica refers to gastric neoplasia, a condition that may require nutritional support and specific dietary management pre- and post-surgery."}{"title": "NEOPLASIA DE COLON:Neoplasia de colon refers to colon neoplasia, which involves dietary considerations and nutritional support following surgical interventions."}{"title": "F\u00cdSTULAS INTESTINALES:F\u00edstulas intestinales are intestinal fistulas that can lead to severe malnutrition and require careful nutritional management and treatment."}{"title": "GASTRECTOM\u00cdA TOTAL:Gastrecom\u00eda total is a surgical procedure that involves the complete removal of the stomach, necessitating specific nutritional management."}{"title": "YEYUNOSTOM\u00cdA DE ALIMENTACI\u00d3N:Yeyunostom\u00eda de alimentaci\u00f3n is a surgical procedure that creates an opening in the jejunum for feeding, often used in patients with gastrointestinal issues."}{"title": "DIETA POLIM\u00c9RICA:DIETA POLIM\u00c9RICA refers to a polymeric diet, which is a form of enteral nutrition designed for patients who can digest food normally. This diet contains whole proteins and offers a balanced mix of nutrients, making it suitable for individuals with specific dietary needs. It is commonly utilized in clinical settings to support the nutritional requirements of patients."}{"title": "DIETA OLIGOPEPT\u00cdDICA:Dieta oligopept\u00eddica is a specialized diet consisting of short-chain peptides, used for patients with malabsorption issues or specific gastrointestinal conditions."}{"title": "GASTRECTOM\u00cdA SUBTOTAL:"}{"title": "P. JUSTO PAVIA:P. Justo Pavia is a medical professional and author who has made significant contributions to the field of medicine, particularly in the areas of polytraumatism, traumatic brain injury, and the care of burn patients. In the referenced text, P. Justo Pavia is noted for contributing to a chapter focused on polytraumatism and traumatic brain injury, as well as another chapter that addresses the management of burn patients and the role of artificial nutrition in their treatment."}{"title": "TRAUMATIC BRAIN INJURY (TCE):Traumatic brain injury (TCE) refers to the brain damage resulting from trauma, which significantly affects the metabolic response and nutritional needs of patients."}{"title": "POLYTRAUMATISMOS:Polytraumatism refers to the condition of having multiple traumatic injuries, which can affect a wide range of patients and requires specialized nutritional support."}{"title": "HARRIS-BENEDICT EQUATION:The Harris-Benedict equation is a formula utilized to estimate an individual's energy requirements, taking into account their weight and activity level. This equation is particularly important for calculating caloric needs, which is essential for determining the nutritional support necessary for patients, especially those experiencing a hypermetabolic state."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL (NE):NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL (NE) refers to nutritional support provided through the gastrointestinal tract. This form of nutrition is particularly essential for patients suffering from severe acute pancreatitis, as it helps meet their dietary needs when they are unable to consume food orally."}{"title": "SEMICYUC:The Spanish Society of Intensive Care Medicine (SEMICYUC) is a medical society dedicated to providing comprehensive guidelines and recommendations for critical care nutrition and metabolic support, particularly for patients who are neurocritical and polytraumatized. The organization has developed specialized recommendations for nutritional approaches in clinical settings, focusing on the management of nutritional needs in critically ill patients, including those with severe burns. SEMICYUC plays a crucial role in collaborating on guidelines that enhance the nutritional support provided to critically ill patients, ensuring that healthcare professionals have access to the best practices in critical care nutrition."}{"title": "BILIOGRAF\u00cdA:The bibliography lists various studies and guidelines related to nutritional support for critically ill patients, emphasizing the importance of tailored nutritional strategies."}{"title": "TCE:TCE, or traumatic brain injury, is a significant medical condition that affects millions of individuals globally each year, leading to considerable rates of death and disability. Recovery from TCE necessitates specific nutritional interventions tailored to support the unique metabolic needs of patients. These nutritional strategies are essential for promoting healing and optimizing recovery outcomes in those affected by this serious condition."}{"title": "HERRERO MESEGUER I:Herrero Meseguer I is a co-author of guidelines for nutritional support in critical care, focusing on neurocritical patients."}{"title": "CONEJERO GARCIA-QUIJADA R:Conejero Garcia-Quijada R is a contributor to the recommendations for nutritional support in critically ill patients, emphasizing the importance of tailored nutrition."}{"title": "BLES MALPICA AL:Blesa Malpica AL is an author of updated recommendations for nutritional support in critically ill patients, particularly those who are polytraumatized."}{"title": "GARCIA DE LORENZO Y MATEOS A:Garcia de Lorenzo y Mateos A is a co-author of guidelines for nutritional support in critically ill patients, focusing on artificial nutrition in polytraumatized patients."}{"title": "MESEJO ARIZMENDI A:Mesejo Arizmendi A is an editor and contributor to guidelines on clinical nutrition and dietetics, particularly in special situations."}{"title": "SINGER P:Singer P is a co-author of the ESPEN Guidelines on Parenteral Nutrition, which provide recommendations for intensive care nutrition."}{"title": "ACOSTA ESCRIBANO J:"}{"title": "PACIENTE S\u00c9PTICO:El paciente s\u00e9ptico es un individuo que presenta una respuesta inflamatoria sist\u00e9mica a una infecci\u00f3n, lo que requiere un tratamiento nutricional espec\u00edfico."}{"title": "HIPERMETABOLISMO:El hipermetabolismo es un estado metab\u00f3lico en el que se movilizan sustratos energ\u00e9ticos como hidratos de carbono y l\u00edpidos para mejorar la funci\u00f3n inmune y la reparaci\u00f3n tisular."}{"title": "HIPERCATABOLISMO:El hipercatabolismo es un proceso en el que se utilizan prote\u00ednas como sustrato energ\u00e9tico, lo que puede llevar a una r\u00e1pida degradaci\u00f3n y p\u00e9rdida de nitr\u00f3geno."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL COMPLEMENTARIA:La nutrici\u00f3n parenteral complementaria se indica en pacientes cr\u00edticos cuando la nutrici\u00f3n enteral no es suficiente para cubrir sus necesidades."}{"title": "COMPLICACIONES SECUNDARIAS:Las complicaciones secundarias son problemas que pueden surgir en pacientes cr\u00edticos si no se inicia la nutrici\u00f3n a tiempo."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N POR SONDA GASTROINTESTINAL:"}{"title": "LIPIDOS:LIPIDOS, or lipids, are a group of organic compounds that are insoluble in water, including fats and oils. They play crucial roles in biological functions and are essential for nutritional support. Lipids provide essential fatty acids and serve as an important non-protein energy source, particularly in infant nutrition. In the context of dietary recommendations, it is noted that lipids should be adjusted in the diet of patients with renal insufficiency, typically comprising 30% of total caloric intake. Overall, lipids are vital for providing energy and maintaining cell membrane structure, highlighting their importance in both health and nutrition."}{"title": "PROTEINAS:Proteins are crucial for daily intake and are catabolized for energy during metabolic stress."}{"title": "ACIDO LINOLEICO:Acido linoleico, also known as linoleic acid, is an essential fatty acid that is crucial for human health. It is recommended for administration in parenteral nutrition to prevent deficiencies in essential fatty acids. As an essential fatty acid, linoleic acid must be included in the diet to ensure adequate nutrition and to avoid potential health issues associated with its deficiency."}{"title": "ACIDO ALFA-LINOLENICO:Alpha-linolenic acid is an essential omega-3 fatty acid important for health."}{"title": "NEOGLUCOG\u00c9NESIS:Neoglucogenesis is the metabolic process of generating glucose from non-carbohydrate substrates, particularly during stress."}{"title": "TCCR:TCCR refers to a specific condition where protein intake may need to be increased to 2-2.5 g/Kg/d\u00eda."}{"title": "ACIDOS GRASOS ESENCIALES:Essential fatty acids, known as \"\u00e1cidos grasos esenciales,\" are vital nutrients necessary for the proper functioning of the human body. These include linoleic and linolenic acids, which are crucial for maintaining health and must be obtained through diet, as the body cannot synthesize them. A deficiency in essential fatty acids can lead to various health issues, including conditions such as hepatic steatosis. Therefore, ensuring an adequate intake of these fatty acids is important for overall well-being."}{"title": "CALORIMETR\u00cdA INDIRECTA:CALORIMETR\u00cdA INDIRECTA is a method used to estimate and measure energy expenditure in patients, making it a crucial tool for managing nutrition, particularly in acute pancreatitis and critically ill patients. It is considered the gold standard for calculating energy requirements in these populations. This method involves measuring oxygen consumption and carbon dioxide production to estimate caloric expenditure, which is essential for determining nutritional needs in various patient groups, including post-operative and oncological patients. \n\nIndirect calorimetry is particularly beneficial for evaluating the energy needs of obese patients and is preferred for calculating nutritional requirements in critically ill individuals. However, despite its advantages, indirect calorimetry is often unavailable in hospitals due to cost and time constraints, limiting its widespread use. Overall, CALORIMETR\u00cdA INDIRECTA serves as a valuable tool in clinical settings for assessing patients' energy expenditure and guiding nutritional interventions."}{"title": "GLUCEMIA:GLUCEMIA refers to the concentration of glucose in the blood, a critical parameter in the management and diagnosis of diabetes, prediabetes, and related complications. Regular monitoring of blood glucose levels is essential for patients undergoing treatment for diabetes and malnutrition, as well as for those receiving parenteral nutrition. It is particularly important to assess glucemia before, during, and after exercise for individuals with diabetes, as dietary intake significantly influences glucose levels. \n\nIn the context of diabetes management, glucemia is crucial for diagnosing conditions such as diabetes and cetoacidosis diab\u00e9tica, and it plays a key role in assessing metabolic health, especially in patients with specific conditions like MELAS syndrome. Blood glucose levels are also tested during the initial assessment of patients with eating disorders to monitor metabolic health and potential complications. \n\nMonitoring glucemia is vital for maintaining glucose levels within normal ranges, particularly for patients with Glycogen Storage Disease I. In clinical practice, blood sugar levels are typically controlled every 4 to 6 hours during the initial days of fasting to detect hypoglycemia, although the level of glucemia may not directly correlate with the effectiveness of dietary interventions. Overall, maintaining appropriate glucemia is essential for the health and management of individuals with diabetes and related metabolic disorders."}{"title": "GL\u00daCIDOS:GL\u00daCIDOS, also known as carbohydrates, are macronutrients that serve as a primary source of energy and are included in nutritional recommendations for patients. However, in the context of a ketogenic diet, the intake of GL\u00daCIDOS is restricted to maintain the desired ketogenic ratio. This highlights the dual role of GL\u00daCIDOS in nutrition, where they are essential for energy but may be limited in specific dietary plans to achieve particular health goals."}{"title": "B.BALERDI P\u00c9REZ:B. Balerdi P\u00e9rez is an author contributing to the chapter on respiratory failure in critically ill patients."}{"title": "P.JUSTO PAV\u00cdA:P. Justo Pav\u00eda is an author contributing to the chapter on respiratory failure in critically ill patients."}{"title": "A.NAVARRO EDUARDO:A. Navarro Eduardo is an author contributing to the chapter on respiratory failure in critically ill patients."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD PULMONAR CR\u00d3NICA:Chronic lung disease that often leads to malnutrition due to various factors including increased basal metabolic rate and respiratory effort."}{"title": "HIPOXIA TISULAR:Tissue hypoxia that can occur in patients with chronic lung disease, contributing to malnutrition."}{"title": "INFLAMACI\u00d3N CR\u00d3NICA:Chronic inflammation that affects nutritional status in patients with respiratory diseases."}{"title": "AUMENTO DEL GASTO BASAL:Increased basal metabolic rate due to respiratory effort and treatments in critically ill patients."}{"title": "BETA-ADREN\u00c9RGICOS:Medications that can affect muscle mass and immune response in critically ill patients."}{"title": "CORTICOIDES:Corticosteroids, commonly referred to as corticoides, are a class of steroid hormones utilized in the treatment of a variety of medical conditions. They are particularly effective in managing acute adrenal insufficiency and serve as anti-inflammatory medications for inflammatory bowel diseases (IBD), often used alongside nutritional support. Key corticosteroids such as dexamethasone, prednisolone, and methylprednisolone are employed to enhance appetite and alleviate nausea in cancer patients, although they are associated with several side effects.\n\nIn the context of IBD, corticosteroids like prednisolone and budesonide play a crucial role in significantly suppressing inflammation during acute episodes. They are also used in high doses to treat conditions such as graft-versus-host disease (GVHD), where they help inhibit the activity of pro-inflammatory prostaglandins and cytokines. However, their use can exacerbate the adverse effects of chemotherapy, including nausea and vomiting.\n\nCorticosteroids are known to impact carbohydrate metabolism, particularly in transplant patients, and may lead to nutritional issues in individuals with chronic respiratory diseases. Additionally, they can cause high potassium loss and are linked to muscle loss and an increased risk of infections in critically ill patients. Despite their effectiveness, the use of corticosteroids in treating symptoms of IBD can be controversial, highlighting the need for careful consideration in their application. They are also utilized in the treatment of conditions such as Graves' ophthalmopathy, where they are administered in intravenous pulses for optimal results."}{"title": "MUCOSA INTESTINAL:The \"MUCOSA INTESTINAL\" serves as a crucial barrier in the gastrointestinal tract, particularly in the early months of life when it may be compromised, allowing the passage of antigens and potentially leading to food allergies. This intestinal lining can exhibit atrophy and linfangiectasias, conditions that are observable during endoscopic examinations and are significant for patient diagnosis. Furthermore, the integrity of the mucosa intestinal is maintained through enteral nutrition, which plays a vital role in reducing the risk of infections."}{"title": "ATROFIA DEL ENTEROCITO:Atrophy of intestinal cells that can occur without enteral nutrition."}{"title": "TRANSLOCACI\u00d3N BACTERIANA:Bacterial translocation that can lead to infections, which enteral nutrition helps to prevent."}{"title": "MORTALIDAD:MORTALIDAD refers to the rate of death within a population and is influenced by various health conditions and factors. It encompasses a range of contexts, including the increased mortality risk associated with malnutrition in critically ill patients and the significant mortality rates linked to specific diseases. For instance, malnutrition is particularly critical in cancer patients, where it can exacerbate mortality risks. \n\nIn the context of anorexia nerviosa, the mortality rate is notably high, estimated at 5-10%, making it one of the most severe psychiatric disorders. Cardiovascular diseases were responsible for nearly 17 million deaths in 2011, highlighting the serious implications of heart health on mortality. \n\nMortality rates can also be affected by the type of nutritional support provided to patients with acute pancreatitis, where mortality ranges from 5% to 20%, indicating the need for careful management. Additionally, conditions such as sarcopenia, frailty, and severe hypophosphatemia are associated with increased mortality risks, particularly in older adults and those with chronic kidney disease.\n\nHyponatremia has been identified as a significant health risk, with higher mortality rates observed in affected patients. Furthermore, dietary factors, including salt intake and vitamin D levels, play a crucial role in influencing mortality, particularly in older populations. \n\nDiabetes is another major public health concern, being one of the leading causes of death in Western countries, with studies highlighting the increased risk of mortality associated with the disease. Overall, MORTALIDAD is a multifaceted concept that reflects the complex interplay between health conditions, nutritional factors, and demographic variables, all of which contribute to the incidence of death in various populations."}{"title": "ESTANCIA HOSPITALARIA:\"ESTANCIA HOSPITALARIA\" refers to the duration of time a patient spends in the hospital. This period is significant as it can be influenced by various factors, including nutritional status, complications arising during surgery, and specific medical conditions such as hyponatremia. Efforts are often made to reduce the length of hospital stay through appropriate nutritional interventions, such as enteral nutrition, which is designed to be immunomodulatory. The goal of these nutritional strategies is to enhance patient recovery and minimize the time spent in the hospital, thereby improving overall health outcomes."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE DISTR\u00c9S RESPIRATORIO AGUDO:The \"S\u00edndrome de Distr\u00e9s Respiratorio Agudo\" (SDRA) is a critical medical condition characterized by acute respiratory failure, which significantly impacts a patient's ability to breathe. This severe syndrome often necessitates the use of mechanical ventilation to support respiratory function. In addition to respiratory support, patients with SDRA may require specialized nutritional attention and the administration of immunomodulatory formulas to aid in their recovery. Overall, SDRA represents a serious health challenge that demands comprehensive medical management and intervention."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDOS GRASOS:\u00c1CIDOS GRASOS, or fatty acids, are essential components of dietary lipids that are classified based on their structure, specifically their chain length and degree of saturation. They play a significant role in nutrition and health, particularly concerning cardiovascular diseases. These nutrients are crucial for energy storage and cellular function, serving as the building blocks of lipids. Fatty acids are also important for the absorption of water and electrolytes, and they contribute to energy support for the lungs, including the synthesis of pulmonary surfactant.\n\nIn nutritional contexts, fatty acids such as ALA (alpha-linolenic acid), EPA (eicosapentaenoic acid), and DHA (docosahexaenoic acid) are recognized for their positive influence on cardiovascular health. They are included in various nutritional formulas due to their vital roles in maintaining overall health and supporting cellular functions. Additionally, fatty acids are produced during the metabolism of triglycerides, further underscoring their importance in energy metabolism and physiological processes."}{"title": "ACEITES DE PESCADO:Aceites de pescado, or fish oils, are recognized for their high content of omega-3 fatty acids, which are beneficial for enhancing the nutritional status of patients experiencing respiratory distress. These oils are frequently utilized in clinical nutrition products, where they can influence both taste and odor. Additionally, fish oils have been extensively researched for their potential effects on blood pressure, further highlighting their significance in dietary and health-related applications."}{"title": "HIPERNUTRICI\u00d3N:Hipernutrici\u00f3n refers to the condition of receiving excessive nutrition, which can lead to complications in patients."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO LA FE:Hospital Universitario la Fe is a healthcare institution in Valencia, Spain, known for its guidelines on artificial nutrition in adults."}{"title": "GENERALITAT VALENCIANA:The Generalitat Valenciana is the regional government of Valencia, Spain, tasked with overseeing health and nutrition policies as well as public health policies. This governmental body plays a crucial role in managing and implementing health-related initiatives within the region, ensuring the well-being of its citizens through effective governance and policy-making."}{"title": "COPD:Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) is a common and progressive lung disease characterized by breathing difficulties due to blocked airflow. It is often associated with long-term exposure to harmful substances, such as irritating gases or particulate matter, which can lead to significant morbidity and mortality. COPD encompasses a group of lung diseases that not only affect respiratory function but also require nutritional support for management. This condition is a significant health issue in various regions, including Spain, where it contributes notably to the overall burden of disease in the population. Additionally, COPD is sometimes studied in relation to other respiratory conditions, such as cystic fibrosis, highlighting its relevance in the broader context of lung health."}{"title": "INTENSIVE CARE UNIT:The Intensive Care Unit (ICU) is a specialized department within hospitals dedicated to the intensive treatment and monitoring of critically ill patients. It is designed to provide advanced medical care and support for individuals who require close observation and complex interventions due to severe health conditions."}{"title": "SDRA:SDRA, or Acute Respiratory Distress Syndrome, is a severe medical condition characterized by respiratory failure. Management of SDRA often necessitates the use of specialized nutritional formulas to support the patient's recovery and overall health."}{"title": "NUTRICION ARTIFICIAL:NUTRICION ARTIFICIAL, or artificial nutrition, refers to the provision of nutrients through means other than oral intake, commonly utilized in critically ill patients. This treatment modality is particularly important for patients with conditions such as inflammatory bowel disease, where it aims to enhance nutritional intake and assist in the remission of the disease."}{"title": "ARGININE:Arginine is a conditionally essential amino acid that plays a significant role in various clinical settings, particularly in immunonutrition. It is known for its immunomodulatory effects, notably in stimulating T lymphocyte activity and reducing pro-inflammatory cytokines. This amino acid is often included in formulas designed for patients with specific deficiencies, such as CPS (carbamoyl phosphate synthetase) and OTC (ornithine transcarbamylase) deficiencies. Additionally, arginine serves as a precursor for nitric oxide, making it a consideration for patients suffering from acute lung injury. Furthermore, it is utilized in the chronic treatment of patients with MELAS (mitochondrial encephalomyopathy, lactic acidosis, and stroke-like episodes) to help manage associated symptoms. Overall, arginine's diverse applications highlight its importance in both immunological and metabolic health."}{"title": "MICRONUTRIENTS:Micronutrients are essential dietary components, including vitamins and minerals, that play a crucial role in various bodily functions. They are vital for modulating inflammation, supporting cardiovascular health, and reducing oxidative stress, which is particularly important for brain health. Micronutrients are also critical in maintaining cognitive function and preventing cognitive decline, especially in older adults. \n\nCertain populations, such as patients post-bariatric surgery, may experience deficiencies in these essential nutrients due to dietary restrictions. Similarly, individuals with Phenylketonuria may require supplementation of specific micronutrients. Additionally, micronutrients are important for patients with respiratory issues and those suffering from conditions like pancreatitis, where deficiencies in nutrients such as thiamine, folic acid, and zinc can occur.\n\nFurthermore, micronutrients like copper, selenium, and zinc are essential for immune modulation and wound healing, particularly in burned patients. The significance of micronutrient intake and its implications for public health are emphasized, highlighting their role in preventing frailty and maintaining overall health."}{"title": "VITAMINS A, C, E:Vitamins A, C, and E are antioxidants that are important for immune function and may be beneficial in patients with respiratory conditions."}{"title": "FOSFORO:Fosforo, also known as phosphorus, is an essential mineral that plays a critical role in various bodily functions, particularly in bone health and energy production. The recommended daily intake of fosforo ranges from 700 to 3,000 mg, depending on individual needs. It is crucial for daily nutrition, and specific intake levels are particularly important for patients, especially those with conditions such as respiratory failure, where phosphorus levels are closely monitored. Overall, fosforo is vital for maintaining overall health and supporting metabolic processes."}{"title": "VENTILACION MECANICA:Mechanical ventilation is a life-support technique used for patients with severe respiratory failure, often requiring specialized nutritional management."}{"title": "ENFERMOS:ENFERMOS refers to pediatric patients who are critically ill and require enteral nutrition. The primary objective of their treatment is to ensure their well-being, which involves providing specialized nutritional support tailored to their specific health needs during their recovery process."}{"title": "HIPERCAATABOLISMO:Hypercatabolism is a state of increased metabolic rate that can occur in critically ill patients, affecting their nutritional needs."}{"title": "AGENTES ANTIOXIDANTES:Antioxidants are substances that may protect cells from damage, and their intake is important for patients with respiratory issues."}{"title": "ALFA-TOCOFEROL:Alpha-tocopherol is a form of vitamin E that is important for antioxidant defense in critically ill patients."}{"title": "NUTRICION:NUTRICION encompasses a vital aspect of health, particularly in the context of medical treatments such as hematopoietic cell transplantation. It plays a crucial role in the preparation and recovery of patients, helping to prevent malnutrition and enhance their quality of life. Additionally, Nutrison Advanced Cubison, a nutritional product developed by Nutricia, is specifically designed to provide dietary support. The field of nutrition also includes the establishment of intervention guidelines aimed at addressing malnutrition risks among frail elderly patients. Furthermore, nutritional studies are conducted to examine dietary intake and its effects on health, utilizing various survey methods to gather data. Overall, NUTRICION is integral to improving health outcomes across different populations, particularly those at risk of malnutrition."}{"title": "CHEST:CHEST is a prominent medical journal dedicated to the publication of research and reviews concerning chest diseases. It encompasses a wide range of topics, including critical care and nutrition in the intensive care unit (ICU), as well as the study and treatment of respiratory diseases. The journal addresses specific conditions such as chylothorax and chylous ascites, contributing to the understanding and management of these complex medical issues. Through its comprehensive coverage, CHEST serves as a vital resource for healthcare professionals involved in the care of patients with respiratory and critical care needs."}{"title": "CRIT CARE MED:Crit Care Med is a journal dedicated to the field of critical care medicine, emphasizing both research and clinical practices. It publishes a variety of studies, including those examining energy expenditure in patients with pancreatitis and analyses comparing clinical outcomes and costs associated with early postoperative enteral immunonutrition in surgical patients. The journal serves as a vital resource for advancements and insights in critical care, contributing to the understanding and improvement of patient care in this specialized area of medicine."}{"title": "NEW ENGLAND JOURNAL OF MEDICINE:The New England Journal of Medicine is a prestigious peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes original research articles and reviews across all areas of medicine. It is known for disseminating significant findings, including research on the risks associated with MEN1 and studies on the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease through the Mediterranean diet. The journal plays a crucial role in advancing medical knowledge and informing clinical practice through its rigorous publication standards."}{"title": "PAUL EM:Paul EM is a researcher who has contributed to the field of enteral nutrition in critically ill patients."}{"title": "HEYLAND D:Heyland D is a researcher involved in studies related to nutrition in critically ill patients."}{"title": "MUSCEDERE J:Muscedere J is a researcher who has co-authored studies on nutrition in critically ill patients."}{"title": "WISCHMEYER PE:Wischmeyer PE is a researcher recognized for his significant contributions to the field of nutrition, particularly in the context of critically ill patients. His work focuses on the nutritional needs of patients suffering from severe conditions, including burn injuries. Wischmeyer PE has conducted various trials aimed at understanding and improving nutritional interventions for these vulnerable populations, thereby enhancing their recovery and overall health outcomes."}{"title": "P. JUSTO PAV\u00cdA:P. Justo Pav\u00eda is an author contributing to the chapter on nutrition in renal insufficiency."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA RENAL AGUDA:\"INSUFICIENCIA RENAL AGUDA,\" or acute renal failure (ARF), is a critical medical condition characterized by a sudden loss of kidney function, which can be reversible or irreversible. This condition leads to a significant reduction in glomerular filtration rate, impairing the kidneys' ability to excrete metabolic waste and maintain fluid and electrolyte balance. Acute renal failure often occurs as a complication of various medical conditions, including severe rhabdomyolysis, which may be linked to the use of statins.\n\nPatients experiencing acute renal failure, particularly those in intensive care, have specific nutritional needs that must be addressed to manage their condition effectively. These needs include adjustments in dietary protein and energy intake, tailored to the patient's overall health status and the type of treatment being administered. The management of acute renal failure requires adherence to specific nutritional guidelines to prevent complications and support recovery, especially in critically ill patients who may experience severe hypercatabolism.\n\nIn summary, \"INSUFICIENCIA RENAL AGUDA\" is a serious condition that necessitates immediate medical intervention and careful nutritional management to mitigate its effects on the body and promote recovery."}{"title": "FRA:Acute renal failure (FRA) is a condition that affects the kidneys' ability to filter waste from the blood, requiring specific nutritional interventions."}{"title": "DI\u00c1LISIS:DI\u00c1LISIS is a medical procedure designed to manage kidney function and nutritional needs in patients with renal failure. It performs the essential functions of the kidneys by removing waste products and excess fluid from the blood when the kidneys are not functioning properly. This procedure is crucial for patients experiencing renal insufficiency, as it helps to eliminate harmful substances and maintain fluid balance in the body.\n\nThere are two primary types of dialysis: hemodialysis and peritoneal dialysis. Both methods aim to replace the kidney's filtering capabilities, but they differ in their approach and execution. While dialysis is effective in managing kidney-related issues, it may also lead to side effects that can impact the patient's nutritional status, necessitating dietary restrictions and careful monitoring of nutritional needs. \n\nIn summary, DI\u00c1LISIS is a vital treatment for individuals with kidney failure, providing essential support for waste removal and fluid regulation, while also requiring attention to potential nutritional challenges."}{"title": "HIPERTIGLICERIDEMIA:Hypertriglyceridemia is a condition characterized by high levels of triglycerides in the blood, which can complicate the nutritional status of critically ill patients."}{"title": "VITAMINAS HIDROSOLUBLES:Water-soluble vitamins are essential nutrients that can be lost during renal replacement therapies, impacting the nutritional care of patients."}{"title": "CATABOLISMO PROTEICO:CATABOLISMO PROTEICO refers to the metabolic process in which proteins are broken down into amino acids. This process is particularly significant in the context of critically ill patients, as it can be increased under such conditions, thereby impacting their nutritional needs. Understanding catabolismo proteico is essential for managing the dietary requirements of patients, especially those who are critically ill, as their protein breakdown rates may necessitate adjustments in their nutritional intake."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES ELECTROL\u00cdTICAS:Alteraciones Electrol\u00edticas refer to disturbances in electrolyte balance that can occur in patients receiving nutritional support, significantly impacting their overall health. These imbalances are particularly common in critically ill patients, making careful nutritional management essential to restore and maintain electrolyte balance. Dietary plans are designed to prevent potential health issues associated with these electrolyte imbalances, highlighting the importance of monitoring and addressing this aspect of patient care."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN LA UCI:"}{"title": "HEMODI\u00c1LISIS:Hemodialysis is a medical procedure designed to filter waste products and excess fluid from the blood in patients whose kidneys are not functioning properly. This treatment is essential for individuals experiencing renal failure, whether acute or chronic, and is particularly important in advanced stages of chronic kidney disease. Hemodialysis requires central venous access and involves the use of a machine that performs the filtration process. \n\nIn addition to removing waste products, hemodialysis also helps to eliminate excess phosphorus from the blood, which is crucial for managing the health of patients with renal failure. The procedure necessitates specific dietary adjustments and careful nutritional management to support the patient's overall health during treatment. \n\nHemodialysis is commonly employed in clinical settings, such as during a patient's stay in an intensive care unit (UCI), where it is vital for managing acute renal failure. Overall, hemodialysis serves as a critical intervention for patients with kidney dysfunction, ensuring the removal of harmful substances from the bloodstream and maintaining fluid balance."}{"title": "HEMOFILTRACI\u00d3N CONTINUA:Continuous hemofiltration is a renal replacement therapy that requires higher protein intake due to increased losses during the process."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA RENAL CR\u00d3NICA:\"INSUFICIENCIA RENAL CR\u00d3NICA,\" or chronic kidney failure, is a long-term medical condition characterized by the gradual loss of kidney function over time. This condition significantly impacts the kidneys' ability to effectively remove waste and maintain fluid balance, leading to various complications. As kidney function declines, patients may experience issues such as malnutrition, caquexia, and growth problems in children. \n\nChronic renal failure often requires careful management, including dietary restrictions, particularly in protein intake, and supplementation of vitamins and minerals to address nutritional deficiencies. The condition is also associated with cardiovascular risks and can lead to severe complications, necessitating interventions such as dialysis or kidney transplantation in advanced stages. \n\nAdditionally, chronic kidney failure can result in limitations in renal potassium excretion and may manifest as hypervolemic hyponatremia. It is important to note that ongoing kidney damage is a primary factor in the progression of this disease, which can be linked to underlying conditions such as diabetes. Overall, \"INSUFICIENCIA RENAL CR\u00d3NICA\" represents a serious health challenge that requires comprehensive management and monitoring."}{"title": "ENERG\u00cdA:The entity \"ENERG\u00cdA\" encompasses various aspects of energy intake and expenditure, which are crucial for dietary management across different populations, particularly in patients with specific health conditions. Energy intake is vital for individuals with renal failure, necessitating tailored caloric recommendations to support their unique dietary needs. In the context of infants receiving parenteral nutrition, energy is defined as the caloric intake essential for their growth and maintenance. Furthermore, energy is recognized as the capacity to perform work, which is fundamental for all bodily functions and activities, especially in children where it plays a significant role in growth and development.\n\nAdditionally, the concept of energ\u00eda includes the assessment of energy expenditure and requirements, which is particularly important for critically ill patients. Accurate calculations of energy expenditure are also critical for dietary planning in diabetes management. Overall, energ\u00eda is an essential nutritional requirement that varies among individuals and is vital for maintaining vital functions and supporting growth, especially in pediatric patients."}{"title": "AMERICAN SOCIETY FOR PARENTERAL AND ENTERAL NUTRITION:The American Society for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (A.S.P.E.N.) is a professional organization dedicated to advancing the science and practice of clinical nutrition. It provides comprehensive guidelines and education on parenteral and enteral nutrition practices in the United States, catering to both adult and pediatric patients. A.S.P.E.N. develops clinical guidelines for nutrition support therapy, particularly during adult anticancer treatment, hematopoietic cell transplantation, and in critical care settings.\n\nThe organization emphasizes the importance of nutrition screening, assessment, and intervention in adults, including those with acute and chronic renal failure, neurological diseases, and other conditions requiring nutritional support. A.S.P.E.N. also offers recommendations for nutritional support in hospitalized patients, ensuring that healthcare providers have the necessary resources to address malnutrition effectively.\n\nOverall, A.S.P.E.N. plays a crucial role in providing guidelines and support for nutrition therapy, focusing on the needs of patients requiring enteral and parenteral nutrition across various healthcare settings."}{"title": "BROWN RO:Brown RO is a researcher and author with a focus on nutrition in clinical settings. He is involved in studies that compare specialized and standard enteral formulas specifically for trauma patients. Additionally, Brown RO has contributed to research on parenteral nutrition solutions, enhancing the understanding of nutritional support in various medical contexts. He is also an author of clinical guidelines that address nutrition support for patients with renal failure, further demonstrating his expertise and commitment to improving patient care through nutritional strategies."}{"title": "NUTRICION ARTIFICIAL EN PANCREATITIS AGUDA:A chapter discussing artificial nutrition in acute pancreatitis, detailing its characteristics and treatment considerations."}{"title": "M. HIG\u00d3N BALLESTER:M. Hig\u00f3n Ballester is a medical doctor recognized for his contributions to the field of nutrition in critical medical conditions. He has co-authored chapters on artificial nutrition, specifically focusing on its application in both acute pancreatitis and liver diseases. His expertise in these areas highlights his significant role in advancing medical knowledge related to nutritional support in severe health issues."}{"title": "HEMODIALISIS:Hemodialysis is a medical procedure to remove waste products and excess fluid from the blood when the kidneys are not functioning properly."}{"title": "DI\u00c1LISIS PERITONEAL:DI\u00c1LISIS PERITONEAL is a type of dialysis that utilizes the lining of the abdomen to filter waste from the blood, serving as an alternative to hemodialysis for patients with renal failure. This treatment method is specifically designed for individuals with chronic kidney disease, allowing for the removal of bodily waste. It is important to note that peritoneal dialysis requires patients to increase their caloric intake due to the presence of glucose in the dialysis fluid. Overall, DI\u00c1LISIS PERITONEAL provides a viable option for those suffering from kidney insufficiency, leveraging the body's own abdominal lining to facilitate the filtration process."}{"title": "SEMIC:Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Medicina Intensiva, Cr\u00edtica y Unidades Coronarias, which provides guidelines for nutritional interventions in critical care settings."}{"title": "NECESIDAD DE CIRUG\u00cdA DE URGENCIA:Urgent surgical intervention may be required in cases of severe pancreatitis aguda, particularly when complications arise."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE RESPUESTA INFLAMATORIA SIST\u00c9MICA:The \"S\u00edndrome de Respuesta Inflamatoria Sist\u00e9mica\" (Systemic Inflammatory Response Syndrome, SIRS) is a clinical condition that can arise from various severe clinical insults, including acute pancreatitis. It is characterized by a systemic inflammatory response, which may manifest through various clinical signs. In severe cases of pancreatitis, SIRS can lead to a hypermetabolic state, necessitating careful nutritional management to support the affected individual. Additionally, it has been noted that the condition can be mitigated through immunonutrition, particularly in post-surgical patients. Overall, SIRS represents a significant clinical challenge that requires comprehensive management strategies to address its inflammatory and metabolic implications."}{"title": "FALLO ORG\u00c1NICO PERSISTENTE:"}{"title": "ENZIMAS PANCRE\u00c1TICAS:\"ENZIMAS PANCRE\u00c1TICAS\" refers to digestive enzymes produced by the pancreas that play a crucial role in the digestion of food. These enzymes are particularly important for patients suffering from conditions such as pancreatitis, where their levels may be elevated and used to assess the severity of the condition. In cases of pancreatitis, supplementation of pancreatic enzymes may be necessary to aid digestion and improve nutrient absorption due to pancreatic insufficiency. Additionally, pancreatic enzymes are also prescribed to patients with cystic fibrosis to help prevent malnutrition by facilitating proper digestion. Overall, these enzymes are vital for individuals experiencing malabsorption issues, ensuring that they receive adequate nutrition."}{"title": "DIETA ABSOLUTA:The \"DIETA ABSOLUTA\" refers to a medical dietary restriction characterized by the complete cessation of food intake. This absolute diet is often implemented in various medical contexts, particularly in cases of suspected lymphatic injuries and as a preparatory measure for medical procedures. Additionally, it is commonly prescribed for patients experiencing acute pancreatitis during the initial treatment phase. The primary purpose of the dieta absoluta is to ensure that no food is consumed, allowing for necessary medical interventions and recovery processes."}{"title": "FLUIDOS IV:Fluidos IV are intravenous fluids administered to patients to maintain hydration and electrolyte balance, especially in cases of acute pancreatitis."}{"title": "ANALG\u00c9SICOS:Analgesics are medications used to relieve pain, which are often required for patients suffering from acute abdominal pain due to pancreatitis."}{"title": "ATB:ATB refers to antibiotics, which may be administered to patients with acute pancreatitis to prevent or treat infections."}{"title": "SCREENING NUTRICIONAL:Screening nutricional is the process of assessing a patient's nutritional status to determine the need for nutritional support in the context of acute pancreatitis."}{"title": "DIETA L\u00cdQUIDA:DIETA L\u00cdQUIDA refers to a dietary phase that is primarily indicated for patients who are recovering from surgery or fasting. This phase consists of easily digestible liquids, allowing individuals to gradually initiate oral tolerance. Additionally, DIETA L\u00cdQUIDA is also applicable for patients who have experienced an episode of acute pancreatitis, as it permits the consumption of clear liquids while they begin to tolerate oral intake. Overall, DIETA L\u00cdQUIDA serves as a crucial step in the recovery process, facilitating a safe transition back to regular dietary habits."}{"title": "DIETA RICA EN HIDRATOS DE CARBONO Y POBRE EN L\u00cdPIDOS:This diet is recommended for patients recovering from pancreatitis to minimize pancreatic stimulation and promote healing.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "CIRROSIS HEP\u00c1TICA:Cirrhosis hep\u00e1tica, or hepatic cirrhosis, is a late-stage liver disease characterized by extensive scarring (fibrosis) of the liver, which is often irreversible. This chronic condition can arise from various liver diseases and conditions, including hepatitis, chronic alcoholism, and glucogenosis due to prolonged liver damage. Cirrhosis can lead to significant complications, such as ascitis quilosa, a condition involving fluid accumulation in the abdominal cavity, and digestive hemorrhage, particularly complicating medical procedures like the placement of gastrostomy tubes. \n\nAdditionally, cirrhosis can affect the body's ability to clear prolactin, which may have further implications for health. Management of cirrhosis often requires dietary modifications, such as salt restriction, to help induce a negative sodium balance and manage symptoms. Overall, cirrhosis hep\u00e1tica represents a serious health concern that necessitates careful monitoring and treatment to mitigate its complications."}{"title": "CARCINOMA HEPATOCELULAR:Carcinoma hepatocellular, also known as hepatocellular carcinoma, is a primary malignancy of the liver that is frequently linked to chronic liver disease and cirrhosis. This type of liver cancer can also arise in patients with hereditary hemochromatosis, especially in the presence of cirrhosis."}{"title": "HEPATITIS V\u00cdRICAS:Viral hepatitis refers to liver inflammation caused by viral infections, which can lead to chronic liver disease."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON:Enfermedad de Wilson, also known as Wilson's disease, is a rare genetic disorder related to copper metabolism, first described in humans in 1912. It is caused by mutations in the ATP7B gene, leading to excessive accumulation of copper in the body. This accumulation primarily affects the liver and the central nervous system, but it can also impact other organs such as the kidneys and cornea. The disorder is inherited in an autosomal recessive manner, meaning that both parents must carry the gene mutation for a child to be affected.\n\nIndividuals with Enfermedad de Wilson may experience a range of health complications, including liver disease, neurological symptoms, and systemic effects, with symptoms often appearing in individuals under 40 years of age. Dietary control of copper intake is essential for managing the condition and preventing serious health issues. The disorder is characterized by decreased biliary excretion of copper, which contributes to its harmful buildup in the body. Overall, Enfermedad de Wilson is a significant health concern that requires careful monitoring and management to mitigate its effects."}{"title": "HEMOCROMATOSIS:Hemochromatosis is a medical condition characterized by excessive iron absorption and accumulation in the body, which can lead to significant health issues. This iron overload primarily affects various organs, including the liver, and can result in severe complications such as liver damage and endocrine dysfunction. The condition may also lead to dysfunction of the parathyroid glands, potentially causing hypoparathyroidism and hypocalcemia. Hemochromatosis can be caused by genetic factors and is often associated with enzymatic deficiencies that result in pathological iron deposits. To manage the condition and prevent complications, dietary control of iron intake is essential. Additionally, it has been noted that hemochromatosis may be related to elevated copper levels in some cases."}{"title": "H\u00cdGADO:The h\u00edgado, or liver, is a vital organ that plays a crucial role in various metabolic processes, including the metabolism of carbohydrates, fats, and proteins. It is primarily responsible for the storage and release of glucose, regulating blood sugar levels, and is involved in the metabolism of galactose and purines. The h\u00edgado also serves as a key site for detoxification, processing harmful substances, and synthesizing bile.\n\nIn addition to its metabolic functions, the h\u00edgado is significant in the storage of essential nutrients, including glycogen, iron, and copper. It plays a role in iron metabolism and is where iron is deposited. The liver is also involved in the urea cycle, which processes nitrogen waste from amino acid metabolism.\n\nThe h\u00edgado can be affected by various diseases, including metabolic disorders such as glucogenosis de tipo I and enfermedad de Von Gierke, where glycogen accumulation occurs. It is also significantly impacted by conditions like hemochromatosis and Wilson's disease, which involves copper accumulation leading to liver failure. The liver's function can be compromised in chronic liver diseases, affecting the overall nutrition and health of the patient.\n\nImaging studies may reveal lesions in the h\u00edgado, indicating potential metastasis or other pathological changes. Additionally, the liver can be influenced by factors such as obesity and nutrition, with its size potentially decreasing significantly with very low-calorie diets prior to surgery.\n\nAs a nutrient-rich organ meat, h\u00edgado provides significant amounts of vitamins and minerals, including iron, and is known to elevate uric acid levels when consumed due to its purine content. Overall, the h\u00edgado is an essential organ that plays a multifaceted role in maintaining metabolic homeostasis and overall health."}{"title": "CIRROSIS:Cirrhosis is a late-stage liver disease characterized by extensive scarring (fibrosis) of the liver, resulting from various liver diseases and conditions, including hepatitis, chronic alcoholism, and hereditary hemochromatosis. This chronic condition can develop from prolonged liver damage and is often exacerbated by complications related to parenteral nutrition, particularly after hepatic steatosis. \n\nCirrhosis leads to significant complications, such as hepatic encephalopathy, fluid retention, hyponatremia, and severe nutritional deficiencies, which are critical considerations in the nutritional assessment of affected patients. The disease is also associated with metabolic complications and can result from the accumulation of copper in the liver, as seen in conditions like Wilson's disease. \n\nOverall, cirrhosis is a severe liver condition that not only impacts liver function but also poses serious risks to the nutritional status and overall health of individuals, making it a significant factor in the prognosis of liver disease."}{"title": "CREATININA:Creatinina, also known as creatinine, is a chemical waste product found in the blood that is primarily used to assess kidney function. It is produced from muscle metabolism and is an important marker in blood tests for evaluating renal health. The measurement of creatinine levels can also provide insights into a person's nutritional status and may influence vitamin D metabolism. Additionally, creatinine levels can be affected in patients with liver disease, highlighting its relevance in broader health assessments. In summary, creatinina is a crucial indicator in blood analyses for evaluating renal function and overall health."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD HEP\u00c1TICA:Enfermedad hep\u00e1tica refers to liver disease, a medical condition that encompasses a range of disorders affecting liver function, including cirrhosis and hepatitis. This condition can significantly impact amino acid metabolism and nutritional status, influencing the energy expenditure and nutritional requirements of affected individuals. Careful nutritional management is essential for those with liver disease, as parenteral nutrition can exacerbate the condition and further affect liver function and health."}{"title": "VARICES ESOF\u00c1GICAS:Esophageal varices are enlarged and swollen veins located in the esophagus. These varices can pose serious health risks, as they have the potential to bleed, which can result in significant blood loss and anemia. Additionally, the presence of esophageal varices can complicate medical procedures, such as the placement of feeding tubes."}{"title": "PLASMA FRESCO:Fresh plasma is used to treat patients with low platelet counts before certain medical procedures."}{"title": "PLAQUETOPENIA:Plaquetopenia, also known as thrombocytopenia, is a condition characterized by a low platelet count in the blood. It is a frequent side effect of the oil of Lorenzo, occurring in approximately 40% of patients who use this treatment. This condition can complicate medical procedures due to the reduced ability of the blood to clot effectively."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N V\u00cdA NASOG\u00c1STRICA:Nasogastric feeding involves placing a tube through the nose into the stomach for nutritional support."}{"title": "FORMULAS POLIM\u00c9RICAS:Polymeric formulas are nutritional solutions used in enteral feeding that contain intact macronutrients."}{"title": "FORMULAS HIPERPROTEICAS:FORMULAS HIPERPROTEICAS are specialized dietary preparations that are high in protein, specifically designed to meet the increased protein requirements of patients with various medical conditions, such as fibrosis qu\u00edstica. These hyperproteic formulas serve as nutritional solutions tailored for specific medical situations, ensuring that individuals receive the necessary protein intake to support their health and recovery."}{"title": "AACR:AACR refers to branched-chain amino acids, which are proposed as a therapeutic option for patients suffering from hepatic encephalopathy. These amino acids are specific nutrients that play a significant role in enteral nutrition for individuals with liver disease."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ORAL:\"NUTRICI\u00d3N ORAL\" refers to the method of feeding that involves the intake of food and liquids through the mouth. This approach is the most common form of nutrition for hospitalized patients and is essential for improving the nutritional status of individuals, particularly after surgeries such as those for gastric cancer. While it is generally the preferred method of nutrient intake, there are circumstances where it may be challenging, such as in cases of acute pancreatitis or liver disease, where the ability to consume food orally can be compromised. Additionally, oral nutrition is recommended for patients with advanced gastric cancer when feasible, and it plays a critical role in the recovery process following liver transplantation. For patients with chronic kidney disease, oral nutrition is aimed at optimizing dietary intake to support their health. Overall, \"NUTRICI\u00d3N ORAL\" is a vital component of patient care, facilitating recovery and maintaining nutritional health across various medical conditions."}{"title": "D\u00c9FICITS DE MICRONUTRIENTES:Micronutrient deficiencies refer to the lack of essential vitamins and minerals in the diet, which can impact health, especially in patients with liver disease."}{"title": "HIG\u00d3N BALLESTER:M.D. Hig\u00f3n Ballester is a medical doctor who contributed to the chapter on short bowel syndrome in the text."}{"title": "ARGENTE PLA:M. Argente Pla is a medical doctor who co-authored the chapter on short bowel syndrome in the text."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN SINDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO:A chapter discussing the nutritional aspects and therapeutic approaches for patients with short bowel syndrome."}{"title": "ESPEN GUIDELINES:The ESPEN Guidelines, established by the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism, offer comprehensive, evidence-based recommendations for nutritional support across a variety of clinical conditions. These guidelines specifically address enteral nutrition for non-surgical oncology patients, patients with dementia, and individuals suffering from liver disease, with the goal of improving patient outcomes. By providing targeted nutritional strategies, the ESPEN Guidelines aim to enhance the overall care and recovery of patients in these diverse medical contexts."}{"title": "VALENCIA:Valencia is a city in Spain that serves as the location for several important institutions and entities. It is home to the Generalitat Valenciana, the regional government of Valencia, and is where the referenced manual was published. Additionally, Valencia hosts significant healthcare facilities, including the Hospital Universitario Doctor Peset and the Hospital Universitario y Polit\u00e9cnico de La Fe. The city is also the site of the Menta publishing house, which published the referenced works."}{"title": "CLIN NUTR:CLIN NUTR, also known as Clinical Nutrition, is a journal dedicated to publishing research related to clinical nutrition. It encompasses a wide range of studies, including those focused on enteral and parenteral nutrition, nutritional support following surgery, and the nutritional aspects of health and disease. The journal addresses various topics, such as muscle contractile and metabolic dysfunction in aging, and has published significant guidelines, including the ESPEN Guidelines on Enteral Nutrition, which cover areas related to liver disease and surgical care. Additionally, CLIN NUTR has published research on clinical nutrition practices and the concurrent validity of the Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool (MUST). Overall, the journal serves as a vital resource for advancing knowledge in nutritional science and its implications in clinical settings."}{"title": "MENTA:"}{"title": "TERAPEUTICA NUTRICIONAL:Therapeutic measures for patients with malabsorption syndrome, including fluid replenishment and specialized nutritional support to prevent malnutrition."}{"title": "NUTRICION ENTERAL:NUTRICION ENTERAL refers to a form of artificial nutrition that is utilized primarily as a treatment for inflammatory bowel disease, particularly in cases of malnutrition. It is recommended to support the adaptation of the remaining intestine following extensive intestinal resection. This approach ensures that patients receive the necessary nutrients directly into the gastrointestinal tract, facilitating recovery and improving overall health outcomes."}{"title": "NUTRICION PARENTERAL:NUTRICION PARENTERAL, or parenteral nutrition, refers to the intravenous administration of nutrients, which allows for the delivery of essential dietary components directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the digestive system. This method is particularly utilized in clinical settings for patients whose energy requirements cannot be adequately met through oral or enteral routes. It is especially beneficial for individuals with significant intestinal resections or other conditions that impair nutrient absorption."}{"title": "LOPERAMIDA:Loperamida, also known as loperamide, is a medication primarily used for treating diarrhea. It works by slowing down gut movement, which helps manage the condition effectively. Loperamida is commonly included in treatment regimens for patients with various types of diarrhea, including those with malabsorption syndrome. It is particularly effective for cases of mild to moderate diarrhea, making it a widely used antidiarrheal medication."}{"title": "SULFATO DE CODE\u00cdNA:Codeine sulfate is an alternative antidiarrheal medication that can be used in conjunction with loperamide."}{"title": "FIBRA:FIBRA, or dietary fiber, is a crucial dietary component that plays a significant role in promoting digestive health and overall well-being. It aids in digestion, improves bowel regularity, and is particularly recommended for managing constipation, especially in patients receiving enteral nutrition. The intake of dietary fiber is linked to a reduced risk of various health issues, including certain cancers, obesity, type 2 diabetes, and cardiovascular diseases. \n\nFiber is essential in pediatric nutrition, often included in formulas to support digestion and health. It is also beneficial for individuals with hereditary fructose intolerance, as it is commonly found in foods that are otherwise restricted. Additionally, fiber can aid in the absorption of water and electrolytes, and it may help prevent diarrhea in enteral nutrition patients.\n\nThe recommended daily intake of dietary fiber is between 20 to 35 grams, which is important for preventing constipation in elderly patients and improving glycemic control and cholesterol levels. Furthermore, fiber has been associated with lower levels of uric acid and a reduced risk of hyperuricemia, making it a valuable component for individuals with diabetes. Overall, FIBRA is recognized for its protective effects against various diseases and its essential role in maintaining digestive health."}{"title": "ACIDOSIS LACTICA:Acidosis l\u00e1ctica, or lactic acidosis, is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of lactic acid in the body, which can occur due to various metabolic disturbances. This condition is particularly relevant in patients with Glycogen Storage Disease I (GSDI), where abnormal glucose metabolism can lead to increased lactate levels in the blood. The buildup of lactic acid is often associated with inadequate oxygen supply to tissues, which exacerbates the condition. \n\nIn addition to GSDI, lactic acidosis can also arise from other metabolic derangements, such as fructose-1,6-bisphosphate deficiency. Furthermore, it can be worsened by the fermentation of unabsorbed carbohydrates in the colon, contributing to malabsorption issues. However, there are potential interventions, such as medium-chain triglyceride (MCT) supplementation, that may help improve the condition. Overall, acidosis l\u00e1ctica is a complex clinical manifestation that requires careful management, especially in individuals with specific metabolic disorders."}{"title": "HIPERSECRECI\u00d3N \u00c1CIDA:Acid hypersecretion is an increase in gastric acid secretion that contributes to malabsorption."}{"title": "RESECCI\u00d3N INTESTINAL:Intestinal resection is a surgical procedure that removes a portion of the intestine, which can lead to malabsorption issues."}{"title": "MALABSORCI\u00d3N:MALABSORCI\u00d3N is a medical condition characterized by the impaired absorption of nutrients from the gastrointestinal tract. This condition can lead to malnutrition and is commonly observed in individuals with various underlying health issues, including inflammatory bowel disease (EII), celiac disease, pancreatic disorders, and liver disease. \n\nPatients with MALABSORCI\u00d3N may experience difficulties in absorbing essential nutrients, which can necessitate dietary adjustments to ensure proper nutrient intake. The condition can also arise as a result of certain medical treatments, such as chemotherapy with cyclophosphamide and radiation therapy, which may further compromise nutritional status. \n\nIn individuals with celiac disease, for instance, the small intestine's inability to absorb nutrients adequately is a significant concern. Similarly, patients with cancer may face challenges related to nutrient absorption, impacting their overall health and recovery. Additionally, medications can influence nutrient absorption, potentially leading to complications such as hypophosphatemia.\n\nOverall, MALABSORCI\u00d3N is a complex condition that requires careful management and dietary planning to address the specific needs of affected individuals."}{"title": "AMERICAN GASTROENTEROLOGICAL ASSOCIATION:The American Gastroenterological Association is a professional organization that focuses on advancing the science and practice of gastroenterology."}{"title": "M.D. HIG\u00d3N BALLESTER:M.D. Hig\u00f3n Ballester is a medical doctor recognized for his contributions to the field of nutrition, particularly in relation to inflammatory bowel disease and cystic fibrosis. He has played a significant role in advancing knowledge and practices surrounding nutritional care for patients with these conditions, demonstrating a commitment to improving health outcomes through specialized dietary interventions."}{"title": "CROHN'S DISEASE:Crohn's disease is a type of inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) that causes chronic inflammation of the gastrointestinal tract, affecting various parts of the digestive system. This condition can lead to significant complications, including malabsorption of essential nutrients such as calcium, which can adversely impact bone health. Nutritional management is a critical aspect of addressing Crohn's disease, as it requires specific dietary considerations to help manage symptoms and maintain overall health. The disease is recognized in both English and Spanish, with the Spanish description emphasizing its nature as a form of inflammatory bowel disease that necessitates targeted management."}{"title": "ULCERATIVE COLITIS:Ulcerative colitis is a chronic inflammatory bowel disease that causes inflammation and ulcers in the digestive tract."}{"title": "BICARBONATO:Bicarbonate, also known as bicarbonato, is a chemical compound that plays a crucial role in maintaining the pH balance in the body, with normal levels typically ranging between 22 and 29 mmol/l. It acts as a buffer, helping to regulate acidity and alkalinity in various physiological processes. Bicarbonate is particularly significant in medical contexts, as it is often measured in patients with diabetic ketoacidosis to assess their metabolic status and is used in treatments to correct acidosis. Additionally, it is recognized as an electrolyte that can be affected in patients experiencing secretory diarrhea, potentially leading to electrolyte imbalances.\n\nResearch has also explored the potential effects of bicarbonate on exercise performance and muscle function, indicating its broader relevance beyond just metabolic health. Overall, bicarbonate is an essential substance in both clinical and physiological settings, contributing to the body's homeostasis and being utilized in various medical treatments."}{"title": "COLECALCIFEROL:Colecalciferol, also known as vitamin D3, is a form of vitamin D that is primarily used to correct vitamin D deficiency. It is recommended as a supplement for patients undergoing steroid treatment to prevent osteopenia and osteoporosis. This highlights its importance in maintaining bone health, particularly in individuals at risk due to medication-related side effects."}{"title": "ESTEROIDES:Los esteroides son medicamentos que se utilizan en diversas aplicaciones m\u00e9dicas, incluyendo el tratamiento de pacientes trasplantados y la enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal. Sin embargo, su uso puede conllevar efectos secundarios significativos. Entre estos efectos secundarios se incluyen la diarrea y la hiperglucemia, lo que resalta la importancia de un monitoreo cuidadoso durante su administraci\u00f3n."}{"title": "SUFICIENTE INGESTA CAL\u00d3RICA:Recomendaci\u00f3n para pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal para asegurar que cumplan con sus requerimientos energ\u00e9ticos diarios."}{"title": "SUPLEMENTOS CAL\u00d3RICOS:Adiciones a la dieta recomendadas para pacientes con malnutrici\u00f3n o retraso del crecimiento en la enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal."}{"title": "DIETA BAJA EN FIBRA:The \"DIETA BAJA EN FIBRA\" is a dietary recommendation aimed at managing symptoms in patients experiencing intestinal issues. It is particularly suggested for individuals with symptomatic intestinal strictures or during flare-ups of severe ulcerative colitis. This low-fiber diet helps alleviate discomfort and is tailored to support those with specific gastrointestinal conditions."}{"title": "DIETA BAJA EN GRASA:The \"DIETA BAJA EN GRASA\" is a dietary approach that is recommended to optimize intestinal motility, particularly for patients experiencing digestive issues. This diet is especially beneficial for individuals with Crohn's disease who are dealing with steatorrhea, as it suggests a modification in the intake of triglycerides. By focusing on low-fat food options, this diet aims to alleviate symptoms and improve overall digestive health."}{"title": "CAQUEXIA TUMORAL:CAQUEXIA TUMORAL is a syndrome associated with advanced cancer, characterized by hypercatabolism and mediated by inflammatory cytokines. This condition is often irreversible and complicates nutritional treatment for affected patients. It is a multifactorial syndrome that leads to the progressive loss of skeletal muscle in cancer patients, significantly impacting their quality of life and survival rates. Despite its prevalence in oncological patients, there is limited evidence regarding the influence of nutrition on the progression of CAQUEXIA TUMORAL."}{"title": "FERNANDEZ-BA\u00d1ARES F:Author of a review and consensus on nutritional therapy in inflammatory bowel disease, contributing to the field of clinical nutrition."}{"title": "LOCHS H:Lochs H is a prominent researcher and co-author of the ESPEN Guidelines on enteral nutrition, which offer expert recommendations in the field of clinical nutrition. He has made significant contributions to the understanding of nutritional support, particularly for patients suffering from liver cirrhosis. Additionally, Lochs H is recognized for his involvement in discussions surrounding the ESPEN guidelines as they pertain to gastroenterology, further emphasizing his expertise and influence in the area of enteral nutrition."}{"title": "MALNUTRICI\u00d3N EN C\u00c1NCER:The study of nutritional needs and interventions for cancer patients, highlighting the prevalence and impact of malnutrition on treatment outcomes."}{"title": "OBSTRUCCIONES DE ALTO GRADO:A condition that can occur in patients requiring nutritional intervention, often necessitating parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "FISTULAS:Fistulas are abnormal connections between organs or vessels that can result in high-output drainage, which may significantly impact an individual's nutritional status and treatment. These conditions often necessitate specific nutritional management strategies to address the complications arising from the abnormal connections."}{"title": "MEGACOLON T\u00d3XICO:A severe complication of inflammatory bowel disease characterized by extreme dilation of the colon, often requiring surgical intervention and nutritional support."}{"title": "TUMOR:A tumor is an abnormal mass of tissue that can be either benign or malignant, often associated with cancer. Tumors can lead to various health issues, including weight loss, depending on their location and type. In the case of a 72-year-old woman, a tumor located in her right lung is likely causing paraneoplastic syndrome and is associated with Cushing's syndrome. Additionally, tumors related to acromegaly can result in increased secretion of growth hormone, which contributes to the symptoms of the disease."}{"title": "G\u00c1STRICO:G\u00e1strico refers to gastric tumors which are known to cause significant weight loss in patients."}{"title": "P\u00c1NCREAS:The pancreas is a vital organ involved in digestion and metabolism, playing a crucial role in the secretion of digestive enzymes and fluids containing electrolytes into the small intestine. It can be adversely affected by various conditions, including cancer, which may lead to malabsorption issues and weight loss due to its impact on digestion. Additionally, the pancreas is susceptible to iron accumulation in conditions such as hemochromatosis. It is also a site where carcinoid tumors can develop, contributing to the secretion of serotonin, and where VIPomas and other neuroendocrine tumors may originate. Recently, a 3 cm nodule was identified in the pancreas during an urgent ultrasound examination, highlighting the importance of monitoring this organ for potential abnormalities."}{"title": "PULM\u00d3N NO MICROC\u00cdTICO:Pulm\u00f3n no microc\u00edtico refers to non-small cell lung cancer, which can lead to weight loss as a symptom."}{"title": "PULM\u00d3N MICROC\u00cdTICO:Pulm\u00f3n microc\u00edtico refers to small cell lung cancer, known for causing weight loss among other symptoms."}{"title": "PR\u00d3STATA:Pr\u00f3stata refers to prostate cancer, which can also result in weight loss in patients."}{"title": "COLON:The colon, also known as the large intestine, is a crucial component of the digestive system. It plays a significant role in various metabolic functions, including the fermentation of undigested carbohydrates, which results in the production of short-chain fatty acids and gases. The colon is home to a vast number of intestinal bacteria that contribute to these metabolic processes. Additionally, it is responsible for the reabsorption of water and electrolytes, which is essential for maintaining fluid balance in the body.\n\nHowever, the colon can be affected by health issues such as colorectal cancer, which can lead to symptoms like diarrhea, malabsorption of nutrients, and weight loss. These complications may arise due to factors such as obstruction and the inability to properly absorb nutrients. Overall, the colon is vital for digestion and nutrient absorption, while also being susceptible to various diseases that can impact its function."}{"title": "LINFOMA ALTO GRADO:Linfoma alto grado refers to high-grade lymphoma, a type of cancer that can lead to significant weight loss."}{"title": "SARCOMAS:Sarcomas are a group of cancers that arise in connective tissues and can cause weight loss."}{"title": "LEUCEMIA AGUDA NO LINFOBL\u00c1STICA:Leucemia aguda no linfobl\u00e1stica refers to acute non-lymphoblastic leukemia, which can also lead to weight loss."}{"title": "MAMA:MAMA refers to breast cancer, a condition that can lead to weight loss in some patients. Additionally, MAMA encompasses breast tissue, and it is important to note that obesity is associated with an increased risk of developing postmenopausal breast cancer. This highlights the complex relationship between body weight and breast cancer, emphasizing both the potential effects of the disease on weight and the influence of obesity on cancer risk."}{"title": "LINFOMA BAJO GRADO:Linfoma bajo grado refers to low-grade lymphoma, which can also be associated with weight loss."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTOS:Tratamientos refers to the various medical interventions, such as surgery, radiotherapy, and chemotherapy, that can affect the nutritional status and weight of cancer patients."}{"title": "ACETATO DE MEGESTROL:Acetato de Megestrol is a medication primarily used as an appetite stimulant, particularly in patients experiencing malnutrition, such as those with cancer. It was prescribed to a patient in 2011, resulting in positive effects on appetite in the subsequent years. The medication is known to improve appetite and increase weight in cancer patients; however, it does not contribute to an increase in lean mass or survival rates. Clinical trials have demonstrated its effectiveness in enhancing appetite and weight gain among this patient population."}{"title": "PREDNISONA:Prednisona is a corticosteroid medication that plays a significant role in the treatment of various medical conditions. It is primarily utilized in the management of inflammatory bowel disease, providing rapid relief of symptoms during acute flare-ups. Additionally, Prednisona is effective in reducing inflammation and suppressing the immune system, making it suitable for treating autoimmune conditions. The medication also serves as an antiemetic, helping to alleviate nausea, although its exact mechanism of action in this regard is not well understood. Furthermore, Prednisona can stimulate appetite in patients suffering from cancer-related malnutrition. While it is beneficial for many conditions, long-term use of Prednisona may lead to secondary osteoporosis. Overall, Prednisona is a versatile glucocorticoid that addresses a range of inflammatory and autoimmune disorders."}{"title": "METILFENIDATO:Metilfenidato is a psycho-stimulant used to help increase appetite in patients suffering from malnutrition due to cancer treatments."}{"title": "METOCLOPRAMIDA:Metoclopramida is a medication that has been tested in patients as part of their treatment for regurgitation. It is primarily used to facilitate the passage of feeding tubes through the digestive system and to improve gastric emptying. As a procin\u00e9tico agent, Metoclopramida promotes gastric emptying and stimulates intestinal motility, which can be beneficial in enhancing enteral nutrition tolerance. It is particularly effective in alleviating nausea, a common symptom in cancer patients that can significantly impact their nutritional intake. The medication is often administered in critical care settings and is recommended to be taken with meals to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort. However, it is important to note that Metoclopramida may be associated with the production of diarrhea. Overall, it is a commonly used medication in oncology for managing nausea and vomiting, as well as for treating gastroparesis."}{"title": "PILOCARPINA:Pilocarpina is a medication primarily used to treat xerostomia, or dry mouth, which is often a side effect of cancer treatments and can significantly affect a patient's ability to eat. When administered at doses of 5-10 mg every 8 hours orally, Pilocarpina can have systemic effects, including potential side effects such as sweating and abdominal pain."}{"title": "NISTATINA:Nistatina is an antifungal medication that is primarily used to treat fungal infections. It is often administered in mouthwash form, which has demonstrated effective results in managing these infections. Additionally, Nistatina can be swallowed, providing versatility in its application. This medication is particularly beneficial for patients experiencing xerostomia, a condition that can occur in cancer patients, as it helps address the fungal infections associated with this condition."}{"title": "FLUCONAZOL:Fluconazol is an antifungal medication that is primarily used to treat fungal infections, particularly in cases of systemic infections. It is recommended for use in cancer patients, as these individuals may be more susceptible to infections that can lead to nutritional issues. To minimize gastrointestinal discomfort, it is advised that Fluconazol be taken with meals. Overall, Fluconazol serves as an important therapeutic option for managing various fungal infections when systemic treatment is necessary."}{"title": "ITRACONAZOL:Itraconazol is an antifungal medication utilized to treat a range of fungal infections, especially in immunocompromised patients, such as those with cancer. It plays a significant role in managing infections that can impact the nutritional status of these patients."}{"title": "RECTO:Recto is the final section of the large intestine, which can be impacted by cancer, affecting bowel habits and nutrient absorption."}{"title": "INTESTINO DELGADO:The \"intestino delgado,\" or small intestine, is a crucial component of the human digestive system, primarily responsible for the absorption of various micronutrients and macronutrients. It plays a significant role in nutrient absorption, where enzymes such as \u03b2-galactosidase aid in the digestion of specific sugars like galactose. While the intestino delgado contributes to the production of uric acid, its role in this process is relatively minor compared to other organs. Additionally, the intestino delgado can be adversely affected by conditions such as celiac disease, cancer, and malnutrition, highlighting its importance in overall digestive health and nutrient assimilation."}{"title": "ESTOMAGO:Est\u00f3mago is the organ where food is digested, and its function can be impaired by cancer, leading to symptoms like early satiety and malabsorption."}{"title": "RESOURCE SUPPORT PLUS:RESOURCE SUPPORT PLUS is a nutritional product developed by Nestl\u00e9, specifically designed for patients who require high-energy and high-protein diets. It is available in a variety of flavors, catering to different taste preferences while providing essential dietary support."}{"title": "RESOURCE SUPPORT INSTANT:A nutritional supplement by Nestl\u00e9, available in powder form, designed for patients needing dietary support."}{"title": "PROSURE:PROSURE is a nutritional drink developed by Abbott, specifically formulated to meet the dietary needs of patients requiring additional nutritional support. This supplement provides essential nutrients and is available in multiple flavors and presentations, catering to the diverse preferences of its users."}{"title": "SUPPORTAN DRINK:Supportan Drink is a nutritional beverage produced by Fresenius Kabi, specifically designed to provide energy and protein for patients in need of nutritional support. This product is available in a variety of flavors, catering to different taste preferences while fulfilling its purpose of aiding in the nutritional needs of individuals."}{"title": "FORTICARE:FORTICARE is a nutritional product developed by Nutricia, specifically designed to meet the dietary needs of patients requiring increased nutritional support. It provides a high-calorie and protein-rich formulation, making it suitable for individuals with heightened energy requirements. Available in various flavors, FORTICARE aims to deliver essential nutrients effectively, ensuring that patients receive the dietary assistance they need for optimal health and recovery."}{"title": "PLANTAGO OVATA:Plantago ovata is a natural fiber supplement used as a bulk-forming laxative, commonly recommended for chronic constipation."}{"title": "BISACODILO:Bisacodilo is a stimulant laxative used to treat constipation by stimulating bowel movements."}{"title": "ONDANSETR\u00d3N:Ondansetron, also known as Ondansetr\u00f3n, is an antiemetic medication that serves to prevent nausea and vomiting, particularly those induced by cancer treatments. It functions as a 5HT3 antagonist, effectively reducing the incidence of nausea and vomiting associated with such therapies."}{"title": "ACICLOVIR:Aciclovir is an antiviral medication primarily used to treat infections caused by specific types of viruses, including herpes. It is recommended that Aciclovir be taken with meals to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort. Additionally, it is effective in addressing viral infections that may lead to symptoms such as nausea and aversion to food."}{"title": "MACROGOL:"}{"title": "BROWN JK:Brown JK is an author of a guide by the American Cancer Society regarding nutrition and physical activity during and after cancer treatment."}{"title": "QUIMIO:QUIMIO refers to chemotherapy, a type of cancer treatment that utilizes drugs to target and kill cancer cells. This treatment method is known to present nutritional challenges for patients undergoing therapy, as the side effects of the drugs can impact their ability to maintain a healthy diet."}{"title": "SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL:SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL, or nutritional support, is a vital intervention aimed at enhancing the tolerance to treatment and improving the quality of life for patients suffering from malnutrition. It is particularly crucial for individuals who have undergone metabolic surgery, especially those experiencing complications. Nutritional support plays a significant role in the management of various health conditions, including cancer and dementia, as it helps to improve overall health outcomes.\n\nThis support is designed to meet the dietary needs of patients who are unable to eat normally, including those with intestinal failure and critically ill patients. It encompasses a range of methods and practices to provide nutrition, especially for patients who cannot consume food orally. Nutritional support is also essential in clinical settings for individuals with eating disorders and is particularly important for children who require assistance in meeting their dietary needs.\n\nOverall, SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL is a comprehensive approach to ensuring that patients receive the necessary dietary assistance to enhance their clinical outcomes and overall well-being."}{"title": "PACIENTES QUEMADOS:\"PACIENTES QUEMADOS\" refers to individuals who have suffered from burns and require specialized nutritional management due to their hypermetabolic and catabolic responses following the injury. These patients are particularly vulnerable, as they often experience critical burn injuries that place them at a high risk of malnutrition. Their condition is characterized by hypermetabolism, hypercatabolism, and inflammation, necessitating careful dietary interventions to support their recovery and overall health."}{"title": "CICATRIZACI\u00d3N:CICATRIZACI\u00d3N refers to the process of wound healing, which is particularly crucial for patients who have suffered burns. This healing process necessitates adequate protein intake to support recovery. Additionally, wound healing is essential for patients undergoing surgical procedures, especially those related to head and neck tumors. The effectiveness of cicatrizaci\u00f3n is significantly influenced by nutritional support, highlighting the importance of proper dietary management in promoting recovery for these patients."}{"title": "VITAMINAS A, C Y D:Suplementos recomendados para pacientes quemados, importantes para la funci\u00f3n inmune y la reparaci\u00f3n de heridas"}{"title": "ELEMENTOS TRAZA:Elementos Traza refers to trace elements that are essential for health and are commonly measured in nutritional assessments to evaluate micronutrient status. These trace elements play a crucial role, particularly in the context of aging, as they contribute to various physiological functions. Important nutrients within this category include copper, zinc, and selenium, which may require supplementation in higher doses, especially in patients who have experienced burns, due to their depletion in such conditions. Overall, Elementos Traza are vital components of a balanced diet and are significant for maintaining optimal health."}{"title": "CATECOLAMINAS:CATECOLAMINAS, also known as catecholamines, are hormones produced primarily by chromaffin cells in the adrenal medulla and the adrenal glands. They include key hormones such as adrenaline, noradrenaline, and dopamine. These hormones play a crucial role in the body's stress response, influencing various physiological processes, including lipid metabolism and the metabolic state of critically ill patients. \n\nCatecholamines are particularly significant in the context of certain medical conditions. Their hypersecretion is a characteristic feature of pheochromocytomas, which are tumors of the adrenal glands that can lead to symptoms such as hypertension. The measurement of catecholamines is often utilized in the diagnosis of pheochromocytoma. Additionally, catecholamines are released in response to hypovolemia and sympathetic stimulation, especially in patients who have suffered burns, further impacting their metabolism. They are also released during stress and can affect the metabolic state in patients with acute pancreatitis. Overall, catecholamines are vital hormones that mediate the body's response to stress and various pathological conditions."}{"title": "GLUCORTICOIDES:Glucocorticoides are a class of corticosteroids and steroid hormones that play a crucial role in the treatment of various inflammatory and autoimmune conditions, including Graves' ophthalmopathy. They are primarily produced by the adrenal cortex and are involved in the regulation of metabolism and immune response. These hormones can be secreted in response to stress, particularly in patients with burns, influencing their hypermetabolic response.\n\nWhile glucocorticoids are effective in managing inflammatory conditions, their use can lead to several side effects, including osteoporosis and the development of Cushing's syndrome. Additionally, they may affect insulin resistance, particularly in cystic fibrosis patients, complicating diabetes management. In certain cases, glucocorticoids are utilized to reduce aldosterone production in conditions like hyperaldosteronism. Furthermore, they can be secreted by adrenal tumors, especially functional ones, and they exert an inhibitory effect on the secretion of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH). Overall, glucocorticoids are significant in both therapeutic applications and physiological responses within the body."}{"title": "GLUCAG\u00d3N:GLUCAG\u00d3N is a hormone that plays a crucial role in glucose metabolism by raising blood glucose levels. It is particularly significant in lipid metabolism as well. This hormone is often elevated in critically ill patients and is released in individuals who have suffered burns, contributing to the hypermetabolic response observed in such conditions."}{"title": "FALLO MULTIORG\u00c1NICO:FALLO MULTIORG\u00c1NICO is a medical condition characterized by the failure of multiple organ systems. This condition can arise as a complication of severe acute pancreatitis, where the inflammatory process affects various organs. Additionally, FALLO MULTIORG\u00c1NICO can also occur in patients who have suffered severe burns, leading to the impairment of multiple body systems. The condition highlights the critical nature of organ function and the interconnectedness of bodily systems in response to severe medical stressors."}{"title": "EQUACI\u00d3N DE HARRIS BENEDICT:F\u00f3rmula utilizada para estimar el gasto energ\u00e9tico en pacientes quemados, aunque puede sobreestimar las necesidades"}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA DE CURRERI:F\u00f3rmula que se basa en el porcentaje de superficie corporal quemada y el peso del paciente para estimar requerimientos energ\u00e9ticos"}{"title": "HIPOVOLEMIA:"}{"title": "K. GARCIA MALPARTIDA:K. Garcia Malpartida is an author associated with the chapter on hematopoietic stem cell transplantation."}{"title": "TPH:TPH refers to hematopoietic stem cell transplantation, a medical procedure involving high doses of chemotherapy followed by the infusion of hematopoietic cells."}{"title": "TMO:TMO refers to bone marrow transplantation, a type of hematopoietic stem cell transplantation."}{"title": "TCSP:TCSP refers to peripheral blood stem cell transplantation, another type of hematopoietic stem cell transplantation."}{"title": "TSCU:TSCU refers to umbilical cord blood transplantation, a type of hematopoietic stem cell transplantation."}{"title": "EICH:EICH, or Graft-versus-Host Disease (GVHD), is a significant complication that can arise following hematopoietic cell transplantation, including stem cell transplants. This condition manifests in both acute and chronic forms and occurs when the transplanted immune cells (the graft) attack the recipient's (the host's) tissues. EICH can lead to various health issues, affecting the patient's metabolism and overall well-being.\n\nPatients experiencing EICH may require specific dietary considerations, particularly those undergoing treatments such as hematopoietic cell transplants. The condition can be influenced by factors such as mucositis and the administration of glutamine treatment. It is crucial for healthcare providers to monitor and manage the nutritional needs of patients with EICH to support their recovery and mitigate complications.\n\nIn summary, EICH is a serious complication of hematopoietic stem cell transplantation that necessitates careful attention to both medical and nutritional management to enhance patient outcomes."}{"title": "EVOH:EVOH, which stands for hepatic veno-occlusive disease, is a complication that can arise following hematopoietic stem cell transplantation. This condition, known in Spanish as \"Enfermedad Vascular Obstructiva del H\u00edgado,\" can also affect transplant patients and necessitates appropriate nutritional management."}{"title": "MUCOSITIS:Mucositis is an inflammatory condition affecting the mucous membranes, particularly in the digestive tract, and is commonly induced by chemoradiotherapy in cancer patients. This condition is characterized by inflammation and ulceration of the mucous membranes, leading to significant complications such as dysphagia and difficulties with nutritional intake. It is reported that mucositis has a high incidence rate, occurring in approximately 70% of patients undergoing intensive chemotherapy treatments. \n\nThe condition can severely impact a patient's ability to eat, making nutritional intervention necessary. Mucositis is especially prevalent among patients receiving high-dose chemotherapy and those undergoing radiotherapy, including those who have undergone hematopoietic cell transplants. \n\nManagement strategies for mucositis may include the administration of oral glutamine, which has been shown to reduce the duration and severity of the condition. Overall, mucositis is a painful and challenging side effect of cancer treatments that requires careful attention to ensure adequate nutrition and patient comfort."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD INJERTO CONTRA HU\u00c9SPED:Graft-versus-host disease (EICH), also known as \"ENFERMEDAD INJERTO CONTRA HU\u00c9SPED,\" is a condition that arises in allogeneic transplants, where donor cells attack the recipient's body. This disease primarily affects the skin, liver, and intestines, with an incidence rate ranging from 30% to 40%. It is a significant complication following hematopoietic stem cell transplantation (TPH), highlighting the challenges associated with immune responses in transplant medicine."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD VENOOCLOSIVA HEP\u00c1TICA:Hepatic veno-occlusive disease (EVOH), a complication that can occur after hematopoietic stem cell transplantation, affecting the liver."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD VENOCLOSIVA HEP\u00c1TICA:Complicaci\u00f3n que puede aparecer en trasplantes aut\u00f3logos y alog\u00e9nicos, con una incidencia del 20% de los pacientes, que puede llevar a fallo m\u00faltiple."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL HIPERPROTEICA:Intervenci\u00f3n nutricional que puede ser necesaria en caso de desnutrici\u00f3n previa al trasplante."}{"title": "NPT:NPT, which stands for Nutrici\u00f3n Parenteral Total or Nutritional Parenteral Therapy, is a method of providing nutrition intravenously to patients who are unable to eat or absorb nutrients through their gastrointestinal tract. This nutritional support is particularly crucial for patients during their hospital stay and is also utilized for infants who cannot receive adequate nutrition through oral feeding. NPT is specifically indicated for individuals with conditions such as severe pancreatitis, where oral intake is not possible or tolerated. Overall, NPT serves as a vital intervention for those requiring nutritional support when traditional feeding methods are not feasible."}{"title": "TRASPLANTE AUT\u00d3LOGO:Tipo de trasplante donde las c\u00e9lulas provienen del propio paciente, sin riesgo de EICH."}{"title": "TRASPLANTE ALOG\u00c9NICO:Tipo de trasplante donde las c\u00e9lulas provienen de un donante, con riesgo de EICH."}{"title": "APLASIA MEDULAR:Condici\u00f3n que se presenta en el postrasplante inmediato, relacionada con la reducci\u00f3n de c\u00e9lulas sangu\u00edneas."}{"title": "INFECCIONES:The entity \"INFECCIONES\" encompasses a range of complications that can significantly impact patient health across various medical contexts. Infections are particularly prevalent in patients undergoing different phases of transplantation, especially those who have received hematopoietic cell transplants, due to the immunosuppression associated with these procedures. Additionally, infections are a common concern in critically ill patients, where they can lead to increased morbidity and mortality.\n\nPatients with specific conditions, such as neutropenia\u2014especially in cases of type Ib glycogen storage disease\u2014are at a heightened risk for infections. The elderly population, particularly those who are malnourished, also face significant health risks from infections. Furthermore, infections can complicate the health of patients with chronic liver diseases and are frequently associated with catheter use, leading to serious health issues.\n\nIn surgical patients, infections are a common complication that can hinder recovery and are often evaluated in studies related to nutritional support. Infections can also contribute to the formation of intestinal fistulas, complicating treatment and recovery processes. Moreover, nutritional requirements may be altered in patients with conditions like cerebrovascular disease, which can further influence their susceptibility to infections. \n\nOverall, infections represent a critical health challenge across various patient populations, necessitating careful management and preventive strategies to mitigate their impact on health outcomes."}{"title": "REACCIONES ADVERSAS MEDICAMENTOSAS:Efectos secundarios que pueden ocurrir en pacientes postrasplante debido a la medicaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES METAB\u00d3LICAS:ALTERACIONES METAB\u00d3LICAS se refiere a cambios en el metabolismo que pueden ocurrir en pacientes trasplantados, as\u00ed como en aquellos con enfermedad hep\u00e1tica cr\u00f3nica. Estas alteraciones pueden afectar la salud general de los pacientes, impactando espec\u00edficamente en el manejo de la glucosa, prote\u00ednas y l\u00edpidos en el organismo."}{"title": "EICH CR\u00d3NICA:EICH CR\u00d3NICA, o enfermedad injerto contra hu\u00e9sped cr\u00f3nica, es una forma prolongada de la enfermedad que puede manifestarse en el postrasplante tard\u00edo. Esta condici\u00f3n aparece generalmente despu\u00e9s del d\u00eda 100 del trasplante y se caracteriza por la aparici\u00f3n de infecciones recurrentes y afectaciones en m\u00faltiples \u00f3rganos. Debido a su naturaleza prolongada, la EICH cr\u00f3nica requiere un manejo m\u00e9dico continuo y cuidadoso para abordar sus complicaciones y mejorar la calidad de vida del paciente."}{"title": "TRASPLANTE:The term \"TRASPLANTE\" refers to various medical procedures involving the transfer of cells or organs to treat serious health conditions. One specific type is the hematopoietic cell transplant, which involves the transfer of stem cells to address diseases such as leukemia and other hematological disorders. Additionally, transplant procedures can lead to complications that necessitate specialized nutritional support for patients. Furthermore, transplantation may also be required for individuals suffering from severe liver damage, such as that caused by Wilson's disease. Overall, \"TRASPLANTE\" encompasses a range of surgical interventions aimed at improving health outcomes for patients with critical medical conditions."}{"title": "CICLOFOSFAMIDA:Ciclofosfamida is a medication that serves multiple purposes in medical treatment. It is primarily recognized as an immunosuppressive drug, which is utilized in clinical trials to address inflammatory responses in brain lesions of patients with Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD). Additionally, ciclofosfamida is commonly used in oncological treatments. However, it is important for patients to take this medication with meals to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort. It is also noteworthy that ciclofosfamida can lead to malabsorption and malnutrition in patients, highlighting the need for careful monitoring during its use."}{"title": "CICLOSPORINA:Ciclosporina is an immunosuppressive medication that is primarily used in the treatment of complications following organ transplants. It has been tested for its efficacy in treating alcoholic liver disease (ALD) but has not shown significant clinical benefits. The drug can lead to various side effects, including diarrhea and neurological issues, which may improve upon discontinuation of the medication. Additionally, ciclosporina can contribute to the development of hypomagnesemia in patients undergoing chemotherapy and may cause alterations in lipid metabolism. It is important to note that the levels of ciclosporina in the body can be increased by the consumption of grapefruit juice, and the medication may also interact with weight loss drugs."}{"title": "HIPOMAGNESEMIA:Hypomagnesemia is a medical condition characterized by insufficient levels of magnesium in the body, specifically defined as a plasma magnesium concentration lower than 1.5 mEq/l. This condition is often associated with various factors, including alcohol abuse, severe malnutrition, and nutritional deficiencies. It has been observed in a percentage of patients, particularly those undergoing treatment with certain medications such as cisplatin and cyclosporine, which can adversely affect their overall health. Additionally, hypomagnesemia is linked to an increased risk of mortality in hospitalized patients. In some cases, patients diagnosed with hypomagnesemia have been treated with magnesium supplements to address the deficiency."}{"title": "BIBL:BIBL is a reference to literature or studies related to nutrition and its applications in medical settings"}{"title": "SONDAS NASOG\u00c1STRICAS:Nasogastric tubes used for enteral feeding, which can increase infection risk in immunosuppressed patients"}{"title": "SONDAS NASOYEYUNALES:Nasojejunal tubes used for enteral feeding, which can also increase infection risk"}{"title": "PEG:PEG, or percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy, is a medical procedure designed to facilitate nutrition for patients who are unable to eat adequately by mouth. This method involves placing a feeding tube directly into the stomach, allowing for long-term nutritional support. PEG is particularly beneficial for individuals requiring enteral nutrition, including those with specific medical conditions such as diabetes and MELAS syndrome, where managing nutritional status is crucial. Overall, PEG serves as an essential treatment tool for providing necessary nutrition to patients who cannot consume food orally."}{"title": "TROMBOPENIA:A condition that increases the risk of bleeding, affecting the placement of feeding tubes"}{"title": "NA\u00daSEAS:NA\u00daSEAS refers to the sensation of needing to vomit, which is a common symptom experienced by patients with cancer. This condition can significantly limit their intake of food, thereby impacting their overall nutritional health. Nausea is not only a distressing symptom but also complicates the administration of enteral nutrition, making it a critical concern in the management of patients undergoing treatment. As a side effect of various medications, nausea can further exacerbate the challenges faced by these patients in maintaining adequate nutrition."}{"title": "\u00cdLEO:\u00cdLEO refers to the ileum, which is the final part of the small intestine. This section plays a crucial role in the absorption of various nutrients, including thyroid hormone. Additionally, the term \"ileus\" is associated with a condition that can complicate the administration of enteral nutrition, indicating that issues in the ileum can affect nutritional intake and absorption. Thus, the ileum is significant not only for its role in nutrient absorption but also for its potential complications in medical conditions such as ileus."}{"title": "HLA:HLA, or Human Leukocyte Antigen, is a crucial system of proteins and a group of genes located on chromosome 6 that plays a significant role in the immune system. It is essential for determining compatibility between donors and recipients in organ transplants, ensuring that the body can accept the transplanted tissue. Additionally, HLA is associated with the body's immune response and has implications for susceptibility to various conditions, including autoimmune diseases such as Type 1 Diabetes and allergies, particularly food allergies. The HLA system is characterized by a high frequency of genetic recombination, which is relevant in the context of genetic inheritance, including conditions like congenital adrenal hyperplasia. Overall, HLA is integral to both transplant medicine and the understanding of immune-related health issues."}{"title": "FIBROSIS QUISTICA:Fibrosis qu\u00edstica (Cystic fibrosis) is a genetic disorder that affects the lungs and digestive system, requiring careful nutritional management."}{"title": "NUTRICION EN FIBROSIS QUISTICA:Nutrition in cystic fibrosis focuses on maintaining adequate nutritional status to improve disease course and quality of life."}{"title": "OMEGA 3:Omega 3 is a type of fatty acid that has been extensively studied for its nutritional benefits. It is known for its anti-inflammatory properties, which may contribute to managing symptoms associated with cancer cachexia. However, while there is some evidence supporting its benefits, the use of Omega 3 in specific contexts lacks clear conclusions, indicating that further research may be needed to fully understand its effects and applications."}{"title": "VALORACION NUTRICIONAL:VALORACION NUTRICIONAL refers to the comprehensive process of assessing an individual's nutritional status, which is essential for identifying and managing various health conditions. This assessment is particularly important in specific populations, such as patients with cystic fibrosis, where it involves evaluating dietary intake, clinical status, and biochemical markers to monitor overall health. Additionally, nutritional assessment plays a crucial role in the care of frail elderly individuals, helping to evaluate their nutritional needs and status. Overall, VALORACION NUTRICIONAL is vital for addressing issues like sarcopenia and frailty, ensuring that appropriate interventions can be implemented to improve health outcomes."}{"title": "HISTORIA DIET\u00c9TICA:The \"HISTORIA DIET\u00c9TICA\" is a comprehensive method used to assess an individual's dietary habits over time. It involves conducting extensive interviews to gather detailed information about both current and past dietary practices. This qualitative assessment is particularly important in specific populations, such as patients with cystic fibrosis, where it is conducted every three months to evaluate nutritional intake. The Historia Diet\u00e9tica is often compared with other dietary assessment methods, highlighting its role in providing a thorough understanding of habitual food intake."}{"title": "VALORACION CL\u00cdNICA Y ANTROPOM\u00c9TRICA:Clinical and anthropometric assessment is performed every three months to monitor growth and nutritional status in cystic fibrosis patients."}{"title": "VALORACION HEMATOL\u00d3GICA Y BIOQU\u00cdMICA:Hematological and biochemical assessment is conducted annually to evaluate various health markers in cystic fibrosis patients."}{"title": "GASTO ENERG\u00c9TICO EN REPOSO:The \"GASTO ENERG\u00c9TICO EN REPOSO\" refers to the amount of energy that the body utilizes while at rest. This expenditure can vary among individuals, particularly in patients with specific health conditions such as cancer. The resting energy expenditure (GER) is essential for understanding the energy requirements of the body in a resting state and can be calculated using specific formulas. This calculation is particularly important for determining the energy needs of patients, including those with conditions like cystic fibrosis, where accurate assessment of energy expenditure is crucial for effective management and treatment."}{"title": "FUNCION PULMONAR:Pulmonary function is assessed to determine the severity of respiratory issues in cystic fibrosis patients, influencing nutritional needs."}{"title": "DENSITOMETRIA:Densitometry is a method used to assess bone density and body composition, important in the nutritional evaluation of cystic fibrosis patients."}{"title": "ANTIOXIDANTS:Antioxidants are compounds found in foods that may reduce the incidence of cardiovascular disease. However, the effectiveness of antioxidants when taken as supplements is a subject of debate."}{"title": "FQ:FQ refers to Cystic Fibrosis, also known as Fibrosis Cystic or Fibrosis Qu\u00edstica, which is a genetic disorder that significantly impacts the lungs and digestive system. This condition is characterized by the production of thick and sticky mucus, which can lead to severe respiratory issues and nutritional challenges. Individuals with cystic fibrosis require careful monitoring and treatment of various health parameters, including detailed dietary assessments to manage their nutritional status effectively. The disorder can result in complications such as malnutrition, necessitating specific dietary management and supplementation. Additionally, there are established guidelines that provide consensus on the nutritional needs of patients with cystic fibrosis, emphasizing the importance of tailored dietary strategies to support their health."}{"title": "KREON:Kreon is a medication that the patient is taking to assist in the digestion of food. It is specifically used to provide pancreatic enzymes to individuals with exocrine pancreatic insufficiency, helping to improve their digestive processes."}{"title": "VITAMINS:Vitamins are essential organic compounds that play a crucial role in normal growth and nutrition for both children and adults. They are vital nutrients that may require supplementation in specific circumstances, such as after bariatric surgery, where reduced fat intake can affect absorption. Certain vitamins, particularly lipid-soluble ones like vitamin K, can interact with anticoagulants, exhibiting antagonistic effects, while vitamins A, D, and E may have agonistic effects.\n\nIn clinical settings, vitamins are often included in nutritional solutions to meet the daily requirements of patients, especially those who are critically ill or have specific health conditions. For instance, vitamins B1, C, D, and E are recommended for supplementation in burned patients to support healing and reduce oxidative stress. Additionally, individuals with diabetes, particularly the elderly, may require certain vitamins to address potential deficiencies.\n\nVitamins are also included in dietary reference intakes for various age groups, ensuring that both children and adults receive adequate nutrition. In cases of malabsorption, such as in individuals with celiac disease, certain vitamins may need to be supplemented to prevent deficiencies. Overall, vitamins are integral to maintaining health and supporting recovery in various medical contexts."}{"title": "MCT:MCT, or Medium-Chain Triglycerides, are a type of fat recognized for their quick energy source and various health benefits. They are commonly used in enteral formulas and nutritional products, particularly for individuals with specific dietary needs, such as those with pancreatic issues or chronic pancreatitis. MCTs are easier to digest compared to long-chain triglycerides, making them suitable for patients who may struggle with fat absorption.\n\nIn addition to their use in enteral nutrition, MCTs are included in certain infant formulas to enhance fat absorption and provide essential fatty acids, which are crucial for infant growth and development. They have also been observed to improve metabolic conditions in patients with glycogen storage diseases and can help manage lactic acidosis and hypertriglyceridemia by promoting fatty acid oxidation and reducing glycolysis.\n\nOverall, MCTs serve as a valuable dietary fat that not only provides extra calories for patients with pancreatitis but also supports weight maintenance and overall health in various clinical settings."}{"title": "PANCREATIC ENZYMES:Pancreatic enzymes are essential for the digestive process, playing a crucial role in breaking down nutrients in the gastrointestinal tract. They are particularly important for individuals with conditions such as cystic fibrosis, where pancreatic insufficiency can hinder proper digestion. In these cases, pancreatic enzymes are often supplemented to aid in digestion. Additionally, these enzymes serve as treatments for patients suffering from exocrine pancreatic insufficiency, helping to improve nutrient absorption and overall digestive health."}{"title": "ESSENTIAL FATTY ACIDS:Essential fatty acids are crucial for health, and patients with cystic fibrosis often have deficiencies in these nutrients, particularly DHA and EPA."}{"title": "EICOSANOIDS:Eicosanoids are signaling molecules made from fatty acids, and patients with cystic fibrosis may have a tendency towards pro-inflammatory eicosanoids due to dietary deficiencies."}{"title": "CFRD:Cystic Fibrosis Related Diabetes (CFRD) is a type of diabetes that develops in approximately 25% of patients with cystic fibrosis, characterized by insulin deficiency and resistance."}{"title": "AMERICAN DIABETES ASSOCIATION:The American Diabetes Association (ADA) is a leading professional organization in the United States dedicated to diabetes research, education, and advocacy. Its primary mission is to prevent and cure diabetes while improving the lives of all individuals affected by the condition. The ADA provides comprehensive guidelines and recommendations for the management and treatment of diabetes, including criteria for diagnosing diabetes and prediabetes, as well as specific guidelines for various contexts such as pregnancy and cystic fibrosis-related diabetes.\n\nThe organization emphasizes evidence-based practices and offers clinical practice recommendations, nutrition principles, and standards of medical care in diabetes management. This includes guidelines for nutrition therapy, the use of bariatric surgery for patients with Type 2 diabetes, and management strategies for complications such as diabetic ketoacidosis, diabetic retinopathy, and diabetic neuropathy. The ADA also collaborates on guidelines for the classification and diagnosis of diabetes, including gestational diabetes and Maturity Onset Diabetes of the Young (MODY) types.\n\nThrough its research initiatives and educational resources, the American Diabetes Association aims to enhance diabetes care and promote better health outcomes for individuals living with diabetes."}{"title": "UK CYSTIC FIBROSIS TRUST:The UK Cystic Fibrosis Trust is an organization that offers support and guidelines for managing cystic fibrosis, including recommendations for diabetes screening."}{"title": "A. RAMOS PROL:A. Ramos Prol is a co-author of the chapter discussing the relationship between nutrition and diabetes in cystic fibrosis patients."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO ENZIM\u00c1TICO:Enzymatic treatment that is not recommended to be combined with elemental or polymeric diets due to potential adverse effects on nutrient absorption."}{"title": "ANTIBI\u00d3TICOS:Antibiotics are medications that play a crucial role in the treatment of various infections and are particularly significant in specific patient populations. They can lead to side effects such as diarrhea, especially after their use has been discontinued. In patients with cystic fibrosis, antibiotics are often administered during respiratory exacerbations and can also impact their nutritional management. Additionally, antibiotics may be used prophylactically in patients with glucogenosis to prevent infections. In the context of patients with SIC, antibiotics like metronidazole are utilized to manage infections and related complications. However, it is important to note that long-term use of antibiotics can disrupt intestinal flora, potentially leading to vitamin K deficiency."}{"title": "NE:NE, or Nutrici\u00f3n Enteral, refers to a method of providing nutrition directly through the gastrointestinal tract via a tube. This approach is particularly beneficial for patients who cannot eat by mouth due to various medical conditions, including neurological impairments that affect swallowing. NE encompasses several specific applications, such as nocturnal enteral nutrition, which delivers nutrition during the night, and nutritional enteral feeding, which is often used in severe cases like pancreatitis.\n\nThe method is designed to meet the caloric requirements of patients and is commonly utilized in critical care settings. It is less associated with complications such as hyponatremia compared to parenteral nutrition, making it a preferred option when the digestive tract is functional. Nutritional formulas used in NE are especially important in oncology settings and for patients with swallowing difficulties.\n\nOverall, NE serves as a crucial nutritional support system, ensuring that patients receive the necessary nutrients directly into their stomach or intestines when oral intake is not possible."}{"title": "NP:NP refers to Nutritional Parenteral, a method of providing nutrition intravenously to patients who cannot tolerate enteral feeding, effectively bypassing the gastrointestinal tract. This approach is particularly relevant for patient groups, including those who have undergone abdominal surgery related to digestive neoplasia, and may experience complications such as nausea and pain. In clinical settings, NP has been studied in relation to various factors, including its correlation with hospital stay duration in patients with hyponatremia. Nutritional practices and guidelines for NP emphasize the use of different lipid sources and amino acids to optimize patient care, especially in critical care environments. Overall, NP serves as a vital nutritional support system for patients who are unable to receive adequate nutrition through traditional means."}{"title": "ELECTROLYTES:Electrolytes are essential minerals in the body that carry an electric charge and play a crucial role in maintaining fluid balance and supporting various physiological functions. They are vital for hydration, muscle function, and overall bodily operations. Electrolytes, such as sodium and potassium, are particularly important and need to be monitored in patients receiving nutritional support, including those with diabetes, as their levels can vary based on health status. These minerals are often added to nutritional solutions to ensure that individuals maintain proper electrolyte levels for optimal health."}{"title": "HYPERGLYCEMIA:Hyperglycemia is a medical condition characterized by abnormally high blood glucose levels, often seen in individuals with diabetes when insulin is insufficient. It is marked by an excessive amount of glucose in the blood, which can lead to serious health complications if not managed properly. This condition is particularly concerning for diabetic patients, as well as for those receiving nutritional support, such as total parenteral nutrition, where hyperglycemia can arise as a complication due to excessive glucose infusion.\n\nIn hospitalized patients, hyperglycemia is associated with poor outcomes and is a significant concern in the context of nutritional management and guidelines for diabetes care. It is also relevant in pediatric intensive care, where it is linked to various outcomes in critically ill children. Additionally, hyperglycemia can occur in patients with severe pancreatitis and is discussed in relation to pregnancy by the International Association of Diabetes and Pregnancy Study Groups.\n\nOverall, hyperglycemia requires careful dietary intervention and management to prevent potential complications, making it a critical focus in both clinical and nutritional settings."}{"title": "GASTROPARESIA DIAB\u00c9TICA:A condition affecting diabetic patients that negatively impacts their tolerance to enteral nutrition, often requiring specific feeding strategies."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS NUTRICIONALES:F\u00d3RMULAS NUTRICIONALES refers to specialized nutritional formulas that serve multiple purposes in dietary management. These formulas can be utilized to establish nutritional requirements in situations where indirect calorimetry is not available. Additionally, they are specifically designed for diabetic patients, incorporating modified carbohydrates and an increased fat content to better meet their dietary needs."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL V\u00cdA ORAL:Oral enteral nutrition involves the use of regular food along with oral supplements to meet dietary needs."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS CON ALTO CONTENIDO EN GRASA:Formulas with high fat content are designed for patients requiring lower carbohydrate intake and higher fat for energy."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS CON REPARTO EQUILIBRADO DE NUTRIENTES:Balanced nutrient formulas are designed to provide a specific quality of carbohydrates and fiber for better absorption in diabetic patients."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDOS GRASOS MONOINSATURADOS:\u00c1CIDOS GRASOS MONOINSATURADOS, or monounsaturated fatty acids, are a type of fat recognized for their favorable impact on cardiovascular health. These fats, including notable examples like oleic acid, are integral components of the Mediterranean diet, which is associated with improved cardiovascular outcomes. They are also included in enteral nutrition formulas, highlighting their role in managing diabetes effectively. \n\nThe health benefits of monounsaturated fatty acids can vary based on their dietary sources; for instance, fats derived from virgin olive oil are particularly noted for their positive effects. Overall, these healthy fats are encouraged in dietary recommendations aimed at enhancing lipid profiles and are considered beneficial or neutral concerning cardiovascular risk. Furthermore, they can be consumed without restriction in children's diets, emphasizing their importance for overall health and well-being. Thus, incorporating \u00e1cidos grasos monoinsaturados into daily nutrition is advocated for better cardiovascular health and effective dietary management of diabetes."}{"title": "DIABETES UK:Diabetes UK is a charity organization dedicated to the prevention and management of diabetes in the United Kingdom. It provides evidence-based nutrition guidelines aimed at helping individuals manage their condition effectively and reduce the risk of developing diabetes. Through its initiatives, Diabetes UK plays a crucial role in supporting those affected by diabetes and promoting healthier lifestyles."}{"title": "DIABETES CARE:\"Diabetes Care\" is a journal published by the American Diabetes Association that focuses on various aspects of diabetes management, including clinical research, education, and practice. The journal is dedicated to publishing a wide range of content related to diabetes care, including position statements, clinical studies, and guidelines that address the management and treatment of diabetes and its complications, such as diabetic retinopathy. \n\nIn addition to clinical care, \"Diabetes Care\" emphasizes the importance of nutrition and its impact on diabetes outcomes, publishing research that explores nutritional aspects and their relationship to diabetes management. The journal also covers related conditions, including studies on obesity, hyperglycemia, and parenteral nutrition. Overall, \"Diabetes Care\" serves as a comprehensive resource for healthcare professionals involved in diabetes management, providing valuable insights into research, guidelines, and best practices in the field."}{"title": "DIABETIC MEDICINE:Diabetic Medicine is a journal that publishes research and guidelines related to diabetes management."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA GEN\u00c9RICA:Nutrici\u00f3n Cl\u00ednica Gen\u00e9rica is a company that produces nutritional products for clinical use."}{"title": "FRESENIUS-KABI:Fresenius-Kabi is a global healthcare company that specializes in lifesaving medicines and technologies. The company is particularly known for its nutritional products, which include formulas designed for children and products aimed at diabetes management. Additionally, Fresenius-Kabi focuses on enteral nutrition, offering specialized products such as Diben. Through its diverse range of offerings, Fresenius-Kabi plays a crucial role in providing essential healthcare solutions."}{"title": "ABBOTT:Abbott is a global healthcare company that develops and manufactures a diverse array of healthcare products, encompassing medical devices, diagnostics, and nutritional supplements. The company is particularly known for its extensive range of nutritional products, which includes specialized formulas designed for various health needs. Among its offerings are products such as Jevity Plus HP, Osmolite HN Plus, Vital P\u00e9ptido 1.5, Ensure Plus Advance, and Glucerna, which cater to individuals with specific dietary requirements, including those with diabetes. Abbott also produces energy drinks and various enteral formulas for medical use, demonstrating its commitment to addressing a wide spectrum of nutritional needs. Overall, Abbott stands out as a comprehensive provider of healthcare solutions, with a strong emphasis on nutritional products."}{"title": "GRIFOLS:Grifols is a global healthcare company recognized for its expertise in the production of plasma-derived medicines and a diverse range of nutritional products. The company develops and manufactures various nutritional offerings, including Dietgrif MCT, Dietgrif hiperproteico, Dietgrif Pudding Completo, and Dietgrif Activ Protein Fibra. Grifols also provides specialized nutritional products aimed at patients, including those with diabetes, and produces enteral formulas to support various healthcare needs. Overall, Grifols is committed to advancing healthcare through its innovative therapies and nutritional solutions."}{"title": "ENTERAL NUTRITION:Enteral nutrition is a medical practice that involves the delivery of nutrients directly into the gastrointestinal tract. This method is particularly beneficial for patients who are unable to eat normally due to various health conditions. It is commonly used in individuals with liver disease, diabetes, and those who have experienced burns. Additionally, enteral nutrition plays a crucial role in the care of critically ill patients and is often utilized in postoperative care. By delivering nutrition directly to the stomach or intestines, enteral nutrition ensures that patients receive the necessary nutrients to support their recovery and overall health."}{"title": "PARENTERAL NUTRITION:Parenteral Nutrition is a medical method of providing nutrition intravenously to patients who are unable to obtain nutrition through eating or absorb food through their digestive tract. This approach is particularly crucial for preterm infants and critically ill patients who cannot feed normally. By bypassing the gastrointestinal tract, Parenteral Nutrition delivers essential nutrients directly into the bloodstream, making it an essential intervention for individuals with severe health conditions, such as acute pancreatitis or those who have specific medical needs that prevent oral consumption of food.\n\nThis method is employed in various medical settings when enteral feeding is not possible or sufficient, ensuring that patients receive the necessary nutrition to support their recovery and overall health. Parenteral Nutrition is also relevant for certain diabetes patients who may struggle to consume food orally. Overall, it serves as a vital nutritional support system for individuals facing significant health challenges."}{"title": "GLUCERNA:Glucerna is a brand of nutritional products specifically designed for people with diabetes. It offers balanced nutrition aimed at helping individuals manage their blood sugar levels effectively."}{"title": "DIABETES-SPECIFIC FORMULAS:Diabetes-specific formulas are specialized nutritional products designed to meet the dietary needs of individuals with diabetes."}{"title": "PERSAN FARMA:PERSAN FARMA is a pharmaceutical company based in Spain that is actively involved in the production and sponsorship of various initiatives related to clinical nutrition, particularly for patients with diabetes mellitus and associated chronic conditions. The company has sponsored round table events and scientific forums focused on nutritional diagnosis and treatment, as well as clinical case conferences that emphasize the importance of nutrition in managing diabetes.\n\nPERSAN FARMA is recognized for its commitment to enhancing the training of healthcare professionals through scientific projects and publications. The company produces a range of nutritional products designed to meet the needs of diabetic patients, including NutAvant HP Fibra, NutAvant Plus, NutAvant HC (a high-calorie nutritional beverage), NutAvant Diab\u00e9tica, and NutAvant Plus Diab\u00e9tica. Additionally, PERSAN FARMA manufactures NutAvant Fibra and NutAvant Est\u00e1ndar, further diversifying its product offerings in the nutritional sector.\n\nThe company is represented by a logo featuring an orange four-leaf clover or flower-like symbol, which reflects its identity within the pharmaceutical industry. Through its various initiatives and products, PERSAN FARMA aims to contribute significantly to the field of clinical nutrition and improve the quality of care for patients with diabetes."}{"title": "S. FORCANO SANJU\u00c1N:S. Forcano Sanju\u00e1n is an author who discusses geriatric nutrition and the challenges faced by the elderly population."}{"title": "GERIATRIC POPULATION:The geriatric population refers to older adults, typically those over 75 years old, who may face various health challenges."}{"title": "NOVASOURCE DIABET:Novasource Diabet is a nutritional product specifically aimed at diabetic patients, produced by Nestl\u00e9. It is designed to provide essential nutrients for individuals with diabetes, supporting their dietary needs and overall health."}{"title": "NOVASOURCE DIABET PLUS:Novasource Diabet Plus is an enhanced nutritional product for diabetics, also produced by Nestl\u00e9."}{"title": "RESOURCE DIABET:Resource Diabet is a dietary and nutritional product specifically designed for diabetic patients, produced by Nestl\u00e9. It is available in multiple flavors and is formulated to meet the dietary requirements of individuals managing diabetes."}{"title": "T-DIET PLUS DIABET NP:T-Diet Plus Diabet NP is a nutritional product for diabetics, produced by Vegenat."}{"title": "T-DIET PLUS DIABET IR:T-Diet Plus Diabet IR is another dietary product for diabetics, produced by Vegenat."}{"title": "DIBEN:Diben is a specialized nutritional product designed for patients requiring dietary management, particularly in the context of diabetes. It is produced by Fresenius-Kabi and serves as an enteral nutrition solution tailored to meet the specific dietary needs of individuals managing diabetes."}{"title": "NUTRISON ADVANCE DIASON:Nutrison Advance Diason is a nutritional product for enteral feeding, produced by Nutricia."}{"title": "NUTRISON ADVANCE DIASON LOW ENERGY:Nutrison Advance Diason Low Energy is a low-energy nutritional product for enteral feeding, produced by Nutricia."}{"title": "ANCIANO:Elderly individuals who are at risk of malnutrition due to various physiological and social factors."}{"title": "PLURIPATOLOG\u00cdA:Pluripatolog\u00eda refers to the presence of multiple diseases that affect the nutrition of the elderly, particularly chronic and psychiatric conditions."}{"title": "POLIFARMACIA:Polifarmacia, also known as polypharmacy, is characterized by the concurrent use of five or more medications by an individual, particularly among the elderly population. This practice can significantly impact nutrient absorption and metabolism, potentially leading to adverse health outcomes. Additionally, the use of multiple medications can contribute to frailty in older adults, highlighting the importance of careful management and monitoring of medication regimens in this demographic."}{"title": "POBREZA:Poverty is a cause of nutritional deficits and associated diseases in the elderly."}{"title": "RECOMENDACIONES NUTRICIONALES:\"RECOMENDACIONES NUTRICIONALES\" refers to a set of dietary guidelines designed to promote health and prevent chronic diseases through proper dietary practices. These recommendations encompass various age groups, including specific guidelines for the elderly, which address their unique energy requirements, water needs, and macronutrient distribution. Additionally, \"RECOMENDACIONES NUTRICIONALES\" includes dietary guidelines aimed at children, focusing on fostering health and nutrition from a young age. Furthermore, these recommendations also target the prevention and management of specific health conditions, such as kidney stones and hyperuricemia, highlighting their comprehensive approach to nutrition and health management across different populations."}{"title": "RECOMENDACIONES ENERG\u00c9TICAS EN EL ANCIANO:Energy recommendations for the elderly based on age and gender, detailing daily caloric needs."}{"title": "FAMILIA:The term \"familia\" encompasses the group of individuals who provide essential support to children and elderly individuals in various healthcare contexts. In the case of children, the family is instrumental in the process of enteral nutrition, where their education and training in managing this technique are vital for the child's well-being. For patients requiring home parenteral nutrition, the family plays a crucial role in overseeing the treatment and ensuring adherence to the prescribed regimen. Overall, the family serves as a fundamental support system, actively involved in the care and assistance of both children and elderly individuals in their nutritional needs."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROMES GERI\u00c1TRICOS:S\u00cdNDROMES GERI\u00c1TRICOS refers to a group of clinical conditions that commonly affect the elderly population. These syndromes include delirium, falls, immobility, incontinence, and pressure ulcers, all of which are associated with frailty in older adults. Geriatric syndromes are often interrelated with malnutrition and other health issues, highlighting the complex health challenges faced by this demographic."}{"title": "DETERIORO COGNITIVO:Cognitive decline is a common issue in the elderly that can be exacerbated by malnutrition."}{"title": "HIPOTENSI\u00d3N POSTURAL:Postural hypotension is a condition where blood pressure drops significantly upon standing, often affecting the elderly."}{"title": "ENFERMO:"}{"title": "PACIENTE ANCIANO:El paciente anciano es un individuo que puede presentar alteraciones en la masticaci\u00f3n y degluci\u00f3n, lo que requiere modificaciones en su dieta y atenci\u00f3n especial."}{"title": "DIETA VARIADA:\"DIETA VARIADA\" refers to a varied diet that is crucial for patients, as it ensures they receive a wide range of nutrients necessary for recovery. This type of diet is particularly important for elderly patients, where a varied and nutritionally dense diet is fundamental for their health. It emphasizes the need for small and frequent meals to meet their dietary requirements effectively."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES DE LA MASTICACI\u00d3N:Las alteraciones de la masticaci\u00f3n en pacientes ancianos pueden requerir modificaciones en la textura de los alimentos para facilitar la degluci\u00f3n."}{"title": "ACTIVIDAD F\u00cdSICA:\"ACTIVIDAD F\u00cdSICA\" refers to physical activity, which plays a crucial role in preventing and managing various health conditions, particularly diabetes and chronic diseases in elderly patients. It is essential for maintaining muscle mass and functionality, especially in cancer patients, where it helps preserve physical strength and overall well-being. Additionally, physical activity is a key component in the treatment of frailty syndrome, enhancing functionality and reducing the likelihood of hospital readmissions. It is also integral to nutritional treatment, contributing to improved quality of life for patients. Activities classified as physical activity include any bodily movement that burns calories, such as walking and strength training, which are particularly beneficial for elderly individuals. Overall, physical activity is recognized as one of the four pillars of comprehensive treatment for frailty in the elderly, highlighting its importance in promoting a healthy lifestyle and managing health conditions effectively."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N DIGNA:La alimentaci\u00f3n digna se refiere a la provisi\u00f3n de una nutrici\u00f3n adecuada y respetuosa para ancianos dependientes."}{"title": "DENSIDAD MINERAL \u00d3SEA:\"DENSIDAD MINERAL \u00d3SEA\" refers to bone mineral density (DMO), a crucial measure used to assess bone strength and predict fracture risk, particularly in patients with osteoporosis. It is an important factor in evaluating the risk of osteoporosis and fractures in older adults. Additionally, DMO is often assessed in patients with Anorexia Nervosa to evaluate their bone health. The term also encompasses the amount of mineral matter per square centimeter of bones, which can be influenced by nutritional interventions in various patient populations, including those with respiratory diseases and celiac disease. Furthermore, DMO can improve in children with glycogen storage diseases when dietary recommendations are adhered to. Overall, \"densidad mineral \u00f3sea\" serves as an indicator of bone health, with adequate nutrition playing a significant role in enhancing bone density, especially in geriatric patients."}{"title": "M\u00c9TODOS DE ADMINISTRACI\u00d3N:Los m\u00e9todos de administraci\u00f3n se refieren a las t\u00e9cnicas utilizadas para proporcionar nutrici\u00f3n enteral a los pacientes, que pueden ser continuos o intermitentes."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS ENTERALES:"}{"title": "ENFERMOS GERI\u00c1TRICOS:Los enfermos geri\u00e1tricos son pacientes de edad avanzada que requieren atenci\u00f3n m\u00e9dica especializada debido a m\u00faltiples condiciones de salud y a menudo enfrentan problemas de nutrici\u00f3n."}{"title": "CUIDADOS PALIATIVOS ONCOL\u00d3GICOS:Son cuidados paliativos espec\u00edficos para pacientes con c\u00e1ncer incurable, enfocados en el control de s\u00edntomas asociados al tumor o a su tratamiento."}{"title": "CUIDADOS PALIATIVOS NO ONCOL\u00d3GICOS:Son cuidados paliativos dirigidos a pacientes con enfermedades cr\u00f3nicas avanzadas y procesos degenerativos en fase terminal."}{"title": "G\u00d3MEZ CANDELA C:G\u00f3mez Candela C is a prominent researcher associated with the NADYA group, where they focus on studies related to home parenteral nutrition and home enteral nutrition in Spain. In addition to their research contributions, G\u00f3mez Candela C has authored significant works, including a chapter on nutrition in eating disorders for a medical textbook and guidelines on home artificial nutrition specifically for oncological patients. They have also emphasized the importance of maintaining a balanced omega 6/omega 3 ratio for overall health. Furthermore, G\u00f3mez Candela C serves as an editor for the \"Manual de recomendaciones nutricionales en pacientes geri\u00e1tricos,\" where they contribute to the development of nutritional recommendations for geriatric patients."}{"title": "COS BLANCO AI:Cos Blanco AI is an author of a chapter in the Manual de recomendaciones nutricionales en pacientes geri\u00e1tricos, focusing on artificial nutrition."}{"title": "SALGADO ALBA A:Salgado Alba A is an author of a chapter in the Manual de geriatr\u00eda, discussing comprehensive geriatric assessment."}{"title": "TENA D\u00c1VILA MC:Tena D\u00e1vila MC is an author of a chapter in the Manual de geriatr\u00eda, addressing malnutrition in the elderly."}{"title": "VALERO ZANUY MA:Valero Zanuy MA is an author of a chapter in the Manual de recomendaciones nutricionales en pacientes geri\u00e1tricos, discussing malnutrition in the elderly."}{"title": "WANDEN-BERGHE LOZANO C:Wanden-Berghe Lozano C is an author of a chapter in the Intervenci\u00f3n nutricional en el anciano, focusing on nutritional requirements in the elderly."}{"title": "CASTRO LOZANO MA:"}{"title": "ASTENIA:Astenia is a condition characterized by a state of physical weakness or lack of energy. It is commonly recognized as a symptom associated with advanced cancer, where it is highly prevalent among non-oncological palliative patients. Additionally, astenia can also manifest as a symptom in individuals with celiac disease, further highlighting its association with various health conditions."}{"title": "PALIATIVOS:Palliative care focuses on providing relief from the symptoms and stress of serious illness, aiming to improve quality of life for patients and their families."}{"title": "PACIENCIA:Patients in palliative care often face challenges related to nutrition and symptom management."}{"title": "INTERVENCI\u00d3N NUTRICIONAL:\"INTERVENCI\u00d3N NUTRICIONAL\" refers to the process of evaluating and modifying a patient's diet to enhance their nutritional status, particularly in individuals with specific health challenges such as cancer. This intervention encompasses a range of actions designed to improve nutritional intake and overall health, with a focus on preventing and reversing nutritional deficiencies. It is especially critical for patients at risk of malnutrition, including those who are frail elderly or suffering from obesity and metabolic diseases. Nutritional intervention strategies may also include dietary changes aimed at managing conditions like hypertension, exemplified by approaches such as the DASH diet. Overall, the goal of \"INTERVENCI\u00d3N NUTRICIONAL\" is to improve health outcomes and quality of life for patients through tailored dietary modifications."}{"title": "CONSEJO DIET\u00c9TICO:The \"CONSEJO DIET\u00c9TICO\" refers to dietary advice aimed at enhancing nutritional intake for patients, particularly those dealing with specific health challenges. This intervention includes recommendations on meal frequency, food preparation, and hydration. It is especially beneficial for patients with esophageal cancer, as it assists them in managing symptoms such as dysphagia (difficulty swallowing) and anorexia by making necessary adjustments to their food intake. Overall, the consejo diet\u00e9tico serves as a crucial support system for improving the dietary habits and overall well-being of patients facing these health issues."}{"title": "CONTROL FARMACOL\u00d3GICO:Pharmacological control involves using medications to stimulate appetite and manage symptoms related to malnutrition in patients."}{"title": "COTICOSTEROIDES:Corticosteroids like Prednisone and Dexamethasone are used to stimulate appetite in patients with a life expectancy of more than four weeks."}{"title": "PSICOESTIMULANTES:Psychostimulants such as Methylphenidate are used to enhance appetite but may cause side effects like sleep disturbances and anxiety."}{"title": "PROGEST\u00c1GENOS:Progestogens, including compounds such as Megestrol acetate and levonorgestrel, are a class of hormones that play significant roles in various physiological processes. Megestrol acetate is particularly noted for its effectiveness in increasing appetite and weight in patients, especially those with a life expectancy of more than three months. On the other hand, levonorgestrel, another type of progestogen, can influence androgen levels and has been associated with conditions such as hirsutism. Additionally, progestogens are known to affect sex hormone-binding globulin (SHBG) levels and are integral to the regulation of the menstrual cycle. Overall, progestogens are versatile hormones with important implications for health and medical treatment."}{"title": "CIPROHEPTADINA:Ciproheptadina is a potent antagonist of histamine and serotonin, primarily recognized for its role as an antihistamine. It has been evaluated for its potential to increase appetite and caloric intake, particularly in patients suffering from malnutrition and advanced cancer. While Ciproheptadina has demonstrated some effectiveness in slightly increasing appetite among patients, its overall impact on weight gain is limited. As an antiserotonergic agent, it has been observed to have a modest effect on appetite enhancement, making it a consideration in the management of appetite-related issues in specific patient populations."}{"title": "SULFATO DE HIDRACINA:Sulfato de Hidracina, also known as hydrazine sulfate, is primarily utilized as an appetite stimulant in patients with cancer, although its effectiveness can vary among individuals. Additionally, it functions as an inhibitor of phosphoenolpyruvate carboxykinase, the initial enzyme involved in gluconeogenesis, which may enhance carbohydrate metabolism. This dual role highlights its potential therapeutic applications in managing symptoms related to cancer and metabolic processes."}{"title": "HALOPERIDOL:Haloperidol is a butyrophenone used for vomiting, especially effective in cases related to opioid use."}{"title": "ESCOPOLAMINA:Escopolamina is an anticholinergic medication that acts on the vomiting center and gastrointestinal tract."}{"title": "OCTE\u00d3TRIDO:Octe\u00f3trido is an antisecretory medication effective in providing symptomatic relief for abdominal obstruction."}{"title": "SONDAS ENTERALES:Sondas enterales are tubes used for enteral nutrition when oral intake is insufficient."}{"title": "DIETA ESTANDAR:Dieta estandar is a standard diet designed to meet patient needs while avoiding excessive lactose content."}{"title": "NAUSEAS:NAUSEAS are a symptom characterized by a sensation of unease and discomfort in the stomach, often leading to the urge to vomit. They can manifest in various medical contexts, including as a symptom in patients with acute pancreatitis, where they contribute to a reduction in oral intake. Additionally, NAUSEAS can occur as a gastrointestinal complication in patients receiving enteral nutrition, negatively impacting their overall well-being and the effectiveness of their treatment. They may also indicate underlying issues such as dehydration or physical overexertion. Furthermore, NAUSEAS are recognized as moderate neurological symptoms in patients with hyponatremia, highlighting their significance in a broader range of health concerns. Overall, NAUSEAS are a common symptom that can exacerbate existing health issues and complicate patient care."}{"title": "INFECCI\u00d3N F\u00daNGICA:Infecci\u00f3n f\u00fangica refers to infections caused by fungi, which can lead to various health issues including xerostom\u00eda."}{"title": "INFECCIONES VIRALES:Infecciones virales are infections caused by viruses that can lead to a variety of symptoms, including nausea and vomiting. Additionally, these viral infections have been implicated as potential environmental triggers for the onset of Type 1 Diabetes, suggesting a broader impact on health beyond immediate symptoms."}{"title": "XEROSTOM\u00cdA:XEROSTOM\u00cdA refers to the condition of dry mouth, which is characterized by a lack of saliva. This condition can significantly impact the ability of individuals, particularly cancer patients, to eat and drink comfortably. Xerostom\u00eda is often a side effect experienced by those undergoing cancer treatment, leading to difficulties in maintaining proper nutrition and hydration."}{"title": "HIPODERMOCLISIS:A method of subcutaneous rehydration that is preferred when oral intake is restricted, requiring changes every 4-5 days due to absorption issues."}{"title": "ALPERS DH:Author of a study on nutritional considerations in wasting diseases, contributing to the field of nutritional therapeutics."}{"title": "ASPEN BOARD OF DIRECTORS:The ASPEN Board of Directors is a governing body responsible for establishing and overseeing guidelines and standards related to parenteral and enteral nutrition practices in medical settings. This board plays a crucial role in ensuring that nutrition support therapy is effectively implemented for both adult and pediatric patients. The ASPEN Board of Directors is dedicated to providing comprehensive guidelines that facilitate the appropriate use of nutrition practices, thereby enhancing patient care and outcomes in various clinical environments."}{"title": "BARRERA R:Author of a study on nutritional support in cancer patients, contributing to the field of nutritional therapeutics."}{"title": "DE BLAUW I:Author of a study on metabolic changes in cancer anorexia, contributing to the field of nutritional therapeutics."}{"title": "GISBERT AGUILAR A:Author of a study on asthenia, cachexia, anorexia, and dehydration, contributing to the field of nutritional therapeutics."}{"title": "PLANAS DOMINGO J:Author of a study on cachexia-anorexia, contributing to the field of nutritional therapeutics."}{"title": "SANMART\u00cdN MOREIRA:Sanmart\u00edn Moreira is the editor of clinical guidelines on palliative care published in Madrid by Aran in 2007."}{"title": "PLANAS DOMINGO:Planas Domingo is an author who contributed to the clinical guidelines on caquexia-anorexia published in Madrid by Aran in 2008."}{"title": "RICO PAZOS:Rico Pazos is an author who wrote about nutrition and hydration for terminal patients in a publication edited by G\u00f3mez Sancho in Las Palmas de Gran Canaria in 2003."}{"title": "SCHATTNER:Schattner is an author who discussed enteral nutritional support for cancer patients in a clinical gastroenterology journal in 2003."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARI LA FE:Hospital Universitari La Fe is a hospital located in Valencia, Spain, involved in pediatric artificial nutrition."}{"title": "G\u00d3MEZ SANCHO:G\u00f3mez Sancho is the editor of a publication on advances in palliative care, which includes contributions on nutrition for terminal patients."}{"title": "LAS PALMAS DE GRAN CANARIA:Las Palmas de Gran Canaria is a city located in the Canary Islands, Spain. It is notable for being a hub of medical publications related to palliative care and nutrition. Additionally, the city is home to the Hospital Universitario Insular de Gran Canaria, a significant healthcare facility that contributes to the region's medical services and research."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER AVANZADO Y TERMINAL:The event focuses on symptom control in patients with advanced and terminal cancer, discussing nutritional support and care."}{"title": "ARAN:"}{"title": "REAL DECRETO 1205/2010:The \"REAL DECRETO 1205/2010\" is a royal decree published on September 24, 2010, in Spain, which establishes the framework for the inclusion of special medical dietary foods within the National Health System. This regulation outlines the nutritional standards and composition requirements for various dietary products, including pediatric formulas, ensuring that they meet the specific needs of different age groups. The decree serves to regulate and facilitate access to these specialized foods, thereby enhancing the healthcare provisions related to dietary needs in Spain."}{"title": "L-AMINO\u00c1CIDOS:L-amino acids are synthetic compounds used in various nutritional formulas, particularly for infants and young children."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS PEDI\u00c1TRICAS:Pediatric formulas are specialized nutritional products designed for infants and children, ensuring they meet specific dietary needs."}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS:\"NI\u00d1OS\" refers to children aged 1-18 years, encompassing a critical demographic with specific nutritional needs essential for optimal growth and development. This group is particularly sensitive to energy restrictions and requires tailored dietary recommendations, especially during key developmental periods such as infancy and adolescence. \n\nChildren are the primary consumers of pediatric formulas, which are designed to meet their unique dietary requirements based on age and health status. They are also the main focus of pediatric nutrition, with particular attention given to their growth and nutritional needs. Adequate intake of essential nutrients, such as iodine and calcium, is crucial for their proper growth and development. \n\nIn terms of dietary recommendations, children are the target population for guidelines regarding vitamin D and calcium intake. They may experience specific health issues, such as growth hormone deficiency and central hypothyroidism due to hypopituitarism, and are at risk of malnutrition, necessitating specialized nutritional support to promote healthy growth and development. \n\nChildren with certain conditions, such as congenital saccharase-isomaltase deficiency, must avoid specific carbohydrates to prevent adverse symptoms, and their tolerance may improve with age. Additionally, children under 4 years old are particularly susceptible to food allergies, largely due to their developing immune systems, with a significant number affected by cow's milk protein allergy.\n\nThe nutritional needs of children vary according to their age, weight, and health status, making them a unique population that often requires parenteral nutrition. They are also vulnerable to malnutrition associated with inflammatory bowel disease (IBD), which can lead to delays in growth and sexual development. \n\nRecent studies have shown that children can benefit from ketogenic diets, particularly for the management of epilepsy, demonstrating a significant reduction in seizure frequency. However, they are also at risk for nutrient-drug interactions due to their still-developing detoxification systems. \n\nOverall, \"NI\u00d1OS\" encompasses a diverse group of children whose dietary needs and health considerations are critical for their growth, development, and overall well-being."}{"title": "LACTANTES:LACTANTES refers to infants aged 0-12 months, specifically focusing on those who are exclusively breastfed and have unique nutritional needs that pediatric formulas aim to address. This group includes infants aged 0-6 months, who are highlighted in dietary recommendations due to their specific developmental requirements. Additionally, LACTANTES encompasses infants up to 10 kg who receive standardized nutrition over several days. It is important to note that breastfeeding women, referred to as lactantes, are advised to avoid certain fish due to concerns about mercury content. Furthermore, LACTANTES includes infants who are still breastfeeding and have particular dietary needs for managing conditions such as Maple Syrup Urine Disease (MSUD). Overall, LACTANTES represents a critical focus in dietary guidelines aimed at ensuring the health and nutritional well-being of infants during their early months of life."}{"title": "TRIGLIC\u00c9RIDOS:TRIGLIC\u00c9RIDOS, or triglycerides, are a type of fat (lipid) found in the blood that play a crucial role in energy provision and support various bodily functions. They are primarily synthesized by the liver and can be derived from dietary sources, particularly from the metabolism of carbohydrates such as fructose. Triglycerides are transported in the bloodstream by lipoproteins, including chylomicrons and very-low-density lipoproteins (VLDL).\n\nElevated levels of triglycerides are associated with an increased risk of cardiovascular diseases and can contribute to conditions such as hyperlipidemia and pancreatitis. Monitoring triglyceride levels is essential for individuals with dyslipidemias, those receiving parenteral nutrition, and patients with specific health conditions like primary hypothyroidism and glycogen storage disease type I (GSDI). Dietary factors, including the intake of omega-3 fatty acids and adherence to dietary patterns like the Mediterranean diet, can influence triglyceride levels.\n\nIn summary, triglycerides are a significant component of blood lipids that require careful management to maintain cardiovascular health and prevent potential complications related to elevated levels."}{"title": "DEXTROSA-EQUIVALENTE:Dextrose equivalent (DE) is a measure used to determine the length of dextrin maltose chains in nutritional formulas, impacting digestibility and osmolarity."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS POLIM\u00c9RICAS:F\u00d3RMULAS POLIM\u00c9RICAS are complete nutritional formulas designed for both pediatric and adult patients, often flavored to enhance palatability. These formulas are specifically formulated for individuals who do not have alterations in intestinal absorption or digestion. They consist of whole proteins and are indicated for patients with minimally affected gastrointestinal function. F\u00d3RMULAS POLIM\u00c9RICAS are utilized in enteral nutrition, containing non-hydrolyzed macronutrients that are suitable for patients with adequate intestinal function. These nutritional products are generally well tolerated and are commonly used in critical care settings, making them a standard choice in enteral nutrition."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS OLIGOM\u00c9RICAS:F\u00d3RMULAS OLIGOM\u00c9RICAS son preparaciones nutricionales que contienen prote\u00ednas hidrolizadas, dise\u00f1adas espec\u00edficamente para pacientes con funci\u00f3n digestiva alterada. Estas f\u00f3rmulas son utilizadas en situaciones donde hay alteraciones en la digesti\u00f3n o absorci\u00f3n intestinal, lo que las hace adecuadas para individuos con necesidades diet\u00e9ticas espec\u00edficas. En particular, las f\u00f3rmulas oligom\u00e9ricas, tambi\u00e9n conocidas como f\u00f3rmulas de p\u00e9ptidos, son especialmente beneficiosas para ni\u00f1os que requieren un soporte nutricional adaptado a sus necesidades digestivas particulares."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS ELEMENTALES:F\u00d3RMULAS ELEMENTALES are highly processed nutritional products primarily composed of synthetic amino acids. They are specifically designed for infants and children who suffer from severe allergies or malabsorption issues, particularly in cases where traditional hydrolyzed formulas are ineffective. These formulas are indicated for digestive conditions that do not respond to oligomeric formulas. However, it is important to note that elemental formulas are characterized by their high osmolarity and cost, which raises concerns about their use and suggests that they should be avoided when possible."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS HIPERPROTEICAS:Hyperproteic formulas contain a higher protein content, indicated for specific medical conditions in older children."}{"title": "DENSIDAD CAL\u00d3RICA:DENSIDAD CAL\u00d3RICA refers to the amount of energy provided per volume of formula, which is essential for meeting the dietary needs of children. It is defined as the quantity of calories per milliliter of formula and is classified into three categories: hypocaloric, normocaloric, and hypercaloric. This classification helps in determining the appropriate formula to ensure that children receive the necessary caloric intake for their growth and development."}{"title": "PEDIATR\u00cdA:La pediatr\u00eda es la rama de la medicina que se ocupa de la salud y las enfermedades de los ni\u00f1os. Esta especialidad m\u00e9dica abarca el tratamiento de diversas condiciones, incluyendo trastornos alimentarios y nutricionales, asegurando as\u00ed un enfoque integral en el cuidado de la salud infantil."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS COMPLETAS:Las f\u00f3rmulas completas son preparaciones alimenticias dise\u00f1adas para proporcionar todos los nutrientes necesarios a los pacientes, especialmente en pediatr\u00eda."}{"title": "TABLA 1:TABLA 1 is a comprehensive resource that encompasses various aspects of nutritional management and assessment. It serves as a record tracking the evolution of a patient's weight, height, BMI, and glycemic control over time, which is crucial for monitoring health progress. Additionally, TABLA 1 includes a list of foods that are discouraged in a broad low-sodium diet, emphasizing dietary restrictions for better health outcomes. \n\nIn the context of pediatric care, TABLA 1 presents the main clinical indications for enteral nutrition, highlighting its importance in managing nutritional needs in children. Furthermore, it details various nitrogen solutions used for parenteral nutrition, providing information on their composition and nutritional values, which is essential for healthcare providers in administering appropriate nutritional support.\n\nMoreover, TABLA 1 provides mandatory nutritional information per 100 g/100 ml, ensuring that users have access to standardized data for dietary planning. Lastly, it outlines the Mini Nutritional Assessment-Short Form (MNA-SF) criteria, which are used to evaluate nutritional status, thereby aiding in the identification of individuals at risk of malnutrition. Overall, TABLA 1 serves as a vital tool in the fields of nutrition and dietetics, offering a multifaceted approach to dietary management and assessment."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N ORAL:Alimentaci\u00f3n oral refers to the process of consuming food by mouth. This method may be transitioned to after enteral nutrition in stable patients. It is particularly significant in the management of patients with intestinal failure, as it plays a crucial role in their nutritional care. However, the ability to engage in alimentaci\u00f3n oral can be affected in patients experiencing malnutrition or gastrointestinal issues. Therefore, the safety of oral feeding is often evaluated in patients who have been receiving enteral nutrition to ensure that they can safely consume food through the mouth."}{"title": "TRASTORNOS DE LA CONDUCTA ALIMENTARIA:\"TRASTORNOS DE LA CONDUCTA ALIMENTARIA\" refers to a range of psychological conditions that significantly impact eating behaviors and the relationship individuals have with food. These disorders, which include anorexia nerviosa (AN) among others, are characterized by abnormal or disturbed eating habits. They can complicate the management of obesity and necessitate specialized treatment approaches. Additionally, eating disorders can develop in children who are subjected to prolonged enteral nutrition, further affecting their relationship with food. Overall, \"TRASTORNOS DE LA CONDUCTA ALIMENTARIA\" encompasses various psychological disorders that require careful attention and intervention."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS HIPOCAL\u00d3RICAS:Las f\u00f3rmulas hipocal\u00f3ricas son preparaciones alimenticias que no tienen indicaciones pedi\u00e1tricas espec\u00edficas."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS NORMOCAL\u00d3RICAS:Las f\u00f3rmulas normocal\u00f3ricas son indicadas en la mayor\u00eda de los pacientes pedi\u00e1tricos, proporcionando un aporte cal\u00f3rico adecuado."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS HIPERCAL\u00d3RICAS:F\u00d3RMULAS HIPERCAL\u00d3RICAS son preparaciones nutricionales espec\u00edficamente dise\u00f1adas para ofrecer un alto contenido cal\u00f3rico. Estas f\u00f3rmulas son especialmente \u00fatiles para pacientes que presentan descompensaci\u00f3n hidr\u00f3pica y son utilizadas en situaciones donde hay un aumento de las necesidades cal\u00f3ricas, como en el caso de pacientes con desnutrici\u00f3n. Su objetivo principal es proporcionar la energ\u00eda necesaria para apoyar la recuperaci\u00f3n y el bienestar de estos pacientes."}{"title": "SONDAS G\u00c1STRICAS Y YEYUNALES:Las sondas g\u00e1stricas y yeyunales son dispositivos utilizados para la administraci\u00f3n de nutrici\u00f3n enteral, adapt\u00e1ndose a las necesidades del paciente."}{"title": "\u00cdLEO G\u00c1STRICO:El \u00edleo g\u00e1strico es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica caracterizada por el retraso en el vaciamiento del est\u00f3mago, frecuentemente observado en el periodo postoperatorio inmediato. Esta condici\u00f3n implica una obstrucci\u00f3n en el proceso de vaciamiento g\u00e1strico, lo que puede llevar a la necesidad de nutrici\u00f3n enteral para asegurar la adecuada ingesta de nutrientes."}{"title": "F\u00cdSTULAS PANCRE\u00c1TICAS:Las f\u00edstulas pancre\u00e1ticas son conexiones anormales que pueden formarse entre el p\u00e1ncreas y otros \u00f3rganos, a menudo requiriendo nutrici\u00f3n enteral para evitar la estimulaci\u00f3n de la secreci\u00f3n pancre\u00e1tica."}{"title": "VACIAMIENTO G\u00c1STRICO:"}{"title": "PICA PERCUT\u00c1NEA:Pica percut\u00e1nea is a medical procedure used for gastrostomy in patients, except those with severe thoracic and spinal deformities, malrotation, previous abdominal surgery, obstructions, and esophageal stenosis."}{"title": "SONDAS DE GASTROSTOM\u00cdA:Gastrostomy tubes are medical devices used for feeding patients who cannot eat by mouth, which can be replaced after three months once the gastrocutaneous fistula is formed."}{"title": "SISTEMAS DE INFUSI\u00d3N:Infusion systems are methods used to deliver nutrients to patients, including gravity drip and pump systems, with specific applications in pediatric and critical care."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS:Formulas refer to nutritional solutions designed for infants and children, tailored to their specific dietary needs based on age and health conditions."}{"title": "RN A T\u00c9RMINO:RN a t\u00e9rmino refers to nutritional formulas for full-term newborns when breastfeeding is not possible."}{"title": "RN PRET\u00c9RMINO:RN PRET\u00c9RMINO refers to fortified breast milk or formulas specifically designed for preterm infants. This nutritional support is provided until the infants reach a certain weight or gestational age, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients for healthy growth and development."}{"title": "ESPGHAN COMMITTEE ON NUTRITION:The ESPGHAN Committee on Nutrition is responsible for developing guidelines and recommendations focused on nutrition for infants and children. This committee also offers practical approaches to pediatric enteral nutrition, ensuring that healthcare professionals have the necessary resources to support the nutritional needs of young patients effectively."}{"title": "ESCAPES DEL CONTENIDO G\u00c1STRICO:Gastric content leaks are complications that can occur around the catheter, leading to skin erosion and other issues."}{"title": "FUGAS A PERITONEO:Leaks into the peritoneum are serious complications that can arise from gastrostomy procedures."}ﬂÄ2␀␀␀␀␀=Ç2␀␀␀␀␀LÖ2␀␀␀␀␀Ôà2␀␀␀␀␀ê2␀␀␀␀␀êê2␀␀␀␀␀Æó2␀␀␀␀␀õû2␀␀␀␀␀Í†2␀␀␀␀␀¨ß2␀␀␀␀␀
